\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia \highlight\uc2 , Philippine c.banks  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2  to support  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 153 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Mai 2010\par 05:40\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, May 7 (Reuters) - Central banks in \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the Philippines \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday to support their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as emerging market assets were hit by growing fears that Greece's debt crisis could spread, traders said.\par \par \uc2  The high-yielding Indonesian rupiah <IDR=> fell just over 1 percent to 9,300 per dollar, the lowest in two months.\par \par \uc2  "We suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  started in the morning," said a trader in Jakarta.\par \par \uc2 The Philippine \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also sold dollars to support the peso <PHP=>, which shed 0.9 percent to 45.78 per dollar, traders said.\par \par \uc2 "I wouldn't be surprised if they sell more since they did buy quite a lot at the low 44.00 levels," said a Manila-based dealer.  (Reporting by Kevin Yao; Editing by Kim Coghill)    \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-ASIA-\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (URGENT)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|IF|PHD|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100507e6570007k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
