\par\par \b \uc2 Dow Jones Asia-Pacific Top Stories Sked For May 7\b0\par\par\uc2 1,774 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Mai 2010\par 09:09\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Following are the top Asia-Pacific stories featured on Dow Jones Newswires as of 0700 GMT. Not all stories appear on all wires. Please direct any questions or comments to asianewseds@dowjones.com.\par \par \uc2 MACRO/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /FIXED INCOME:\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: JAPAN: G-7 PLANS TO DISCUSS GREEK TURMOIL IN CONFERENCE CALL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's finance minister said Friday that Group of Seven finance ministers plan to discuss Greece's debt turmoil in a telephone conference later in the day as concerns mount over the broad financial fallout from the beleaguered European nation's troubles. (published 0453 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: AUSTRALIA'S RBA RAISES INFLATION, GDP FORECASTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of Australia\f28 \uc2 \f2  Friday revised up its forecasts for inflation and economic growth, signaling that more interest rate increases will be needed to temper a surge in activity fueled by a hefty commodity price upswing and limited spare capacity. (published 0327 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: CHINA THINK TANK FORECASTS 2ND-QUARTER GDP UP 10.7% - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 An influential Chinese government think tank said the country's brisk first-quarter economic growth will likely slow a tad to 10.7% in the current quarter, but recommended that Beijing allow the yuan to move in a wider trading band to help stem hot money inflows driven by growing international expectations of yuan appreciation. (published 0446 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par KOREA BOND MARKET EXPECTS \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TO STAND PAT - ASSOCIATION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bond-market participants were near-unanimous in expecting the Bank of Korea to leave its key policy rate unchanged during a review due next week amid rising concerns over euro-zone debt, the Korea Financial Investment Association said Friday. (published 0615 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par KOREA GOVERNMENT: EUROPE FISCAL WOES TO HAVE LIMITED DIRECT IMPACT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The South Korean government on Friday said that the fiscal woes of southern European states will have limited direct impact on the domestic financial market. (published 0252 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AUSTRALIAN HOME-LOAN ARREARS RISE IN FEBRUARY - S&P \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 For the second straight month, Australia's home buyers were increasingly unable to pay mortgages underlying prime residential mortgage-backed securities on time in February, according to a \f28 \uc2 \f2 Standard & Poor's\f28 \uc2 \f2  report issued Friday. (published 0319 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: NZ GOVT 9-MONTH CORE OPERATING DEFICIT BEATS FORECASTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The New Zealand government's core operating deficit tracked better than forecast in the nine months ended March 31, but underlying tax revenue remained weak as the country gradually emerges from a prolonged downturn. (published 0228 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: AUSTRALIA PM: MARKETS JUDGE GREEK PLAN TO BE INADEQUATE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's Prime Minister Kevin Rudd said Friday global financial markets have judged the Greek rescue plan as inadequate, and as a result financial market stability will be at the core of the agenda for the forthcoming Group of 20 leaders' meeting in Canada in June. (published 0044 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BANK \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INDONESIA\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TO CONTINUE \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENING\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  - ACTING GOVERNOR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will continue to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market to defend the rupiah, acting Governor Darmin Nasution said Friday. (published 0636 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PHILIPPINES MAY SELL $1B-$1.5B GLOBAL BONDS NEXT YEAR - OFFICIAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Philippines is planning to sell $1 billion to $1.5 billion of global bonds next year to help bridge the country's budget deficit, a senior finance official said Friday. (published 0414 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par RENHE DELAYS PRICING 5-YEAR DOLLAR BOND DUE TO MARKET CONDITION -SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Renhe Commercial Holdings\f28 \uc2 \f2 , a developer of underground shopping malls in China, has decided to delay pricing its five-year dollar-denominated global bond owing to unfavorable market conditions, a person familiar with the plan said Friday. (published 0212 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =PREVIEW: INDONESIA 1Q GDP GROWTH LIKELY ACCELERATED TO 5.78% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indonesia's economic growth likely accelerated in the January-March period to its fastest pace since the third quarter of 2008 as households continued to spend amid benign inflation and companies made more investments on rising confidence on the prospects of the economy, analysts said. (published 0421 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =PREVIEW: MALAYSIA MARCH INDUSTRIAL OUTPUT LIKELY +13.5% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Malaysia's industrial output growth in March was likely substantially stronger than the month before on robust external demand, economists said. (published 0208 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 EQUITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =ASIAN SHARES SLUMP ON WALL ST CUE; AUSSIE SHARES SLIDE TO 8-MO LOWS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asian shares slumped again Friday as Wall Street's slide spooked already-jittery investors, with Australia's market falling to an eight-month low and recent gains in the yen hurting exporter shares in Tokyo. (published 0137 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: CHINA TIAN YUAN MINING SHELVES UP TO US$522M HK IPO - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China Tian Yuan Mining Ltd. has become the latest victim of volatile market conditions and has decided to shelve its up to US$522 million Hong Kong initial public offering indefinitely, a person familiar with the situation said Friday. (published 0414 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 RELIANCE INDUSTRIES\f28 \uc2 \f2  LAWYER: COURT ASKS RIL-RNRL TO RENEGOTIATE PACT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's highest court Friday ruled that a private gas supply agreement between the billionaire Ambani brothers isn't binding, a lawyer for \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reliance Industries Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said. (published 0625 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TOSHIBA SWINGS TO JANUARY-MARCH NET PROFIT ON NAND MEMORY DEMAND \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Toshiba Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Friday it swung to a net profit in the fiscal fourth quarter thanks partly to strong demand for flash memory on the back of the growing popularity of smartphones and other mobile gadgets. (published 0615 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UMC APRIL REVENUE RISES 35.5% ON YEAR TO NT$9.32 BLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Taiwan's \f28 \uc2 \f2 United Microelectronics Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Friday its revenue rose 35.5% in April to NT$9.32 billion, from NT$6.88 billion a year earlier. (published 0655 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: DBS GROUP 1Q NET UP 23%, LOWER THAN EXPECTATIONS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 DBS Group Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., Singapore's largest bank by assets, Friday reported a 23% rise in first-quarter net profit on an increase in non-interest income and an overall improvement in credit quality. (published 0011 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 UNITED OVERSEAS BANK\f28 \uc2 \f2  1Q NET S$700M VS S$409M; EXPECTED S$551.2M \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 United Overseas Bank Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Friday reported a better-than-expected 71% jump in its first-quarter net profit due to a one-time gain from the divestment of its insurance asset and higher non-interest income. (published 0456 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: KAROON SHARES CONTINUE ROLLER COASTER RIDE, JUMP 14% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Shares in \f28 \uc2 \f2 Karoon Gas Australia Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . on Friday defied a rout on global markets to jump 14% after the company got some promising results from a key exploration well and a broker slapped a buy rating on what is one of Australia's most volatile stocks. (published 0613 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: NZ TELECOM 3Q PROFIT FALLS; SOUTHERN CROSS DIVIDEND LOWER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Telecom Corp. of New Zealand Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . reported Friday a 39% fall in third-quarter net profit, hit by a lower contribution from its half-owned cable company and costs arising from outages at its XT mobile network, but the company maintained its guidance for the full year. (published 0337 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: \f28 \uc2 \f2 LG TELECOM\f28 \uc2 \f2  1Q NET UP MORE THAN FIVE-FOLD AT KRW543.2 BLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 LG Telecom Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Friday that its first-quarter net profit jumped more than five-fold from a year earlier, largely on one-off gains from a revaluation of its merged entities. (published 0313 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: ALUMINA SAYS DEMAND IMPROVING; KEEPS COST, OUTPUT GUIDANCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bauxite miner, alumina producer and aluminum smelter \f28 \uc2 \f2 Alumina Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Friday reiterated previous cost and output guidance for 2010 amid an ongoing improvement in global demand for industrial metals. (published 0148 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: ALLIED FARMERS: VALUERS REDUCE PROPERTY ASSETS PURCHASED FROM HANOVER, UNITED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Small New Zealand rural services company \f28 \uc2 \f2 Allied Farmers Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Friday independent valuers have reduced the value of property and loan assets it acquired from Hanover Finance and United Finance in December last year. (published 0349 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ICTSI 1Q NET PROFIT $22.8 MLN VS $11.0 MLN >ICT.PH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 International Container Terminal Services Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Friday its net profit in the first quarter more than doubled to $22.8 million on stronger port \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  amid improving global trade. (published 0340 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: MANDO CORP IPO PRICED NEAR MIDPOINT OF RANGE; RAISES $436.4 MLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korean auto parts maker \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mando Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . on Friday said its initial public offering on the Korea Exchange has been priced at KRW83,000 per share, slightly above the midpoint of the indicative range of KRW75,000 - KRW90,000 per share, raising about $436.4 million in the process. (published 0417 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 JINDAL STEEL\f28 \uc2 \f2 : BOLIVIA FINE, IF LEVIED, CAN'T BE MORE THAN $18 MLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Jindal Steel & Power Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said the Bolivian government can't fine it more than $18 million if it falls short of its investment target in a planned mining project, the company told the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bombay Stock Exchange\f28 \uc2 \f2  in a statement Friday. (published 0439 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PETRON 1Q NET PROFIT PHP1.93 BLN VS PHP874 MLN >PCOR.PH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Petron Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 .,, the Philippines' largest oil refiner by sales and capacity, said Friday that first-quarter net profit more than doubled to PHP1.93 billion on more stable crude oil prices. (published 0655 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ALASKA MILK 1Q NET PROFIT PHP523 MLN VS PHP197 MLN >AMC.PH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Philippine-listed dairy company \f28 \uc2 \f2 Alaska Milk Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Friday its net profit in the first quarter surged to PHP523 million from PHP197 million a year earlier on robust sales amid improving economic conditions. (published 0635 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PILIPINO TELEPHONE 1Q NET PROFIT PHP458 MLN VS PHP3.2 BLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Pilipino Telephone Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Friday its net profit in the first quarter declined to PHP458 million from PHP3.2 billion following the sale of its cellular business to a sister company in August last year. (published 0620 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ADVANCED INFO SERVICE MAINTAINS 2010 REVENUE GROWTH TARGET AT 3% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 07-05-10 0709GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Advanced Info Service PCL\f28 \uc2 \f2 , Thailand's largest mobile phone operator by subscribers, said Friday that it is maintaining its 2010 revenue growth target this year at 3%. (published 0621 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ENERGY/COMMODITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 RELIANCE INDUSTRIES\f28 \uc2 \f2  LAWYER: COURT ASKS RIL-RNRL TO RENEGOTIATE PACT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's highest court Friday ruled that a private gas supply agreement between the billionaire Ambani brothers isn't binding, a lawyer for \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reliance Industries Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said. (published 0625 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SINOPEC\f28 \uc2 \f2  GROUP TO RAISE GAS OUTPUT, IMPORTS, UNCONVENTIONAL GAS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese oil giant \f28 \uc2 \f2 China Petrochemical Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., or Sinopec Group, aims to raise natural gas production and imports as part of its effort to cut carbon emissions, the company said in a report on its website. (published 0504 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par VIETNAM PVEP: PLAN $16.5 BILLION OIL EXPLORATION, PRODUCTION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 PetroVietnam Exploration Production Corp., or PVEP, said Friday that it will invest $16.5 billion in oil exploration and production from 2011 to 2015. (published 0445 GMT) [ 07-05-10 0709GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 62550   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100507e65700104\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
