\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK:Indonesia Shares Likely Lower; 2800 Support Tipped\b0\par\par\uc2 1,338 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Mai 2010\par 04:04\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; \par MarketTalk@dowjones.com \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0204 GMT [Dow Jones] Indonesia shares likely to fall, weighed by weak IDR, concerns over future of nation's economy after Finance Minister Sri Mulyani leaves office, as well as euro-zone debt woes, traders say; tip support at 2800. "We have tons of negative sentiment which I think will push investors to continue to take cash on risk aversion," says trader at Lautandhana Securities; index still up 12% since start of 2010. Car maker Astra (ASII.JK), Bank Rakyat (BBRI.JK) may lead falls on profit-taking. (edhi.pranasidhi@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 0203 GMT [Dow Jones] Copper futures on Shanghai Futures Exchange higher on technical rebound after declines in previous 2 sessions, shrugging off downbeat sentiment from overnight losses in LME counterparts due to renewed worries on sovereign debt problems in Europe, says Orient Securities Futures analyst Ying Haoliang. Adds, improving spot copper prices also lending support. Spot copper currently trades at premium of CNY100-CNY200/ton against front-month SHFE contract, vs discount of CNY100-200/ton last week, indicating increasing buying interest from downstream users. Says Shanghai copper may consolidate with downward bias in coming weeks as worries over further monetary tightening measures by Beijing may re-emerge. Benchmark August copper last +1.2% at CNY57,240/ton. (yue.li@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0201 GMT [Dow Jones] Korea treasury bonds, bond futures higher in early trade as lingering concerns over euro-zone debt problems push investors away from risk assets to safer havens, while Kospi down 1.8%; 3-year yield down 4 bps at 3.67%, 5-year yield down 2 bps at 4.30%, June futures +17 ticks at 111.41. But local securities firm trader notes, "investors seem a bit cautious over the possibility of foreign investors reducing their position in local bonds. It wouldn't be a big problem for those who had hedged their \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  risks, but the sharp rise in the dollar/won could be a disadvantage to foreign investors who had bought local bonds betting on a strong won." Tips 3-year yield in 3.65%-3.69% range. USD/KRW still trading sharply higher at 1,136.7 vs 1,115.5 late Tuesday in Seoul. (min-jeong.lee@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0200 GMT [Dow Jones] GBP/JPY may fall if U.K. general election results in hung parliament in which no party wins majority in 650-seat House of Commons, says \uc2 Global Futures & \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst Akira Maekawa; this may make it difficult for smooth financial rehabilitation in U.K. down road. Dealers say GBP/JPY could decline to 140.50 in near-term vs last 141.92. Separately, EUR/JPY could rise briefly if any comments at ECB rate setting meeting, due later in global day, help allay some fears over euro-zone debt problems; market widely expects no change in interest rate. But adds euro-zone debt problems will remain an issue, which could weigh on unit in longer term. For today, tips EUR/JPY may recover to 120.90 vs last 120.48.(miho.nakauchi@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0200 GMT [Dow Jones] Australian retail sales will likely remain weak for some time as RBA rate hikes impact consumers with prospects of more tightening still ahead, says \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2  Economist Helen Kevans; "those interest rate hikes are really starting to bite." Says sales won't pick up either; "we do think we will continue to see this weakness going forward." (enda.curran@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0159 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/HKD extends gains to 7.7670 vs 7.7665 late yesterday; funds continue switching into USD amid lingering concerns of Greek debt crisis, potential spillover to other eurozone countries, says local trader. Thinks pair could rise even more, but 7.7690 likely immediate resistance, "as IPO-related demand is still quite strong at the moment, counteracting general risk aversion." (aries.poon@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0159 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/CNY up slightly as central parity set higher following USD's overnight gains. Pair at 6.8269 vs 6.8263 late yesterday, central parity at 6.8269 vs 6.8267. "The pair may narrow gains later in afternoon as some banks tend to sell the dollar when the market is about to close on last minute orders from some customers," says Shanghai-based local bank trader. (wynne.wang@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0158 GMT [Dow Jones] Thai shares may open lower as weakness in overseas markets on increased worries over euro-zone debt may trigger some profit-taking. SET index closed +4.4% at 796.86 Tuesday after prime minister proposed reconciliation roadmap Monday; Thai market shut Wednesday for public holiday. "The political tension has been eased, providing some light at the end of the tunnel. If the protesters announce when the protests will be stopped, the market is ready to rise," says KT Zmico Securities' first VP Charoen Iamphattanatham. Adds, if there's any positive news on the political front, banks and medium-sized stocks tipped to gain on value after recent selling pressure as fundamentals remain strong. Energy plays may be weighed by oil price slip. Support at 780. Resistance put at 820 if 800 breached. (piyarat.setthasiriphaiboon@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0157 GMT [Dow Jones] China shares open down led by banks, property developers as persistent monetary tightening concerns, Europe debt woes hurt. Shanghai Composite Index down 1.1% at 2827.24, faces support at psychologically important 2800 level. "The concerns about policy tightening, possible further fund-raising from banks and also weakness from the U.S. and European markets all contribute to the sluggish sentiment," says Qian Qimin from Shenyin Wanguo Securities. \uc2 China Construction Bank Corp\uc2 . (601939.SH) off 1.4% at CNY5.12, Bank of China (601988.SH) off 1.2% at CNY4.08, \uc2 China Vanke Co\uc2 . (000002.SZ) off 2.1% at CNY7.33, \uc2 Poly Real Estate Group\uc2  (600048.SH) off 2.8% at CNY11.11. Shenzhen Composite Index down 0.5% at 1123.60, China May stock index futures down 0.3% at 3068.6.(esther.fung@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0156 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/TWD slips to 31.568 vs 31.600 late yesterday, shrugging off losses in local shares (Taiex down 0.3%) as some foreign investors sell USD on longer-term view that TWD set for gains, says local bank trader; exporters also selling USD for settlement needs. Tips pair in 31.500-31.800 band. "Many investors and exporters are taking the opportunity to sell now as this level is pretty acceptable to them." But suspects \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may buy USD later to prevent too large a TWD gain when stocks are falling. charmian.kok@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0155 GMT [Dow Jones] Aussie bonds' wild ride going to last through the week, says Sally Auld, senior interest rate strategist with \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2 . Aussie bond prices strengthened overnight on Greek debt concerns, pared back some of those gains on better-than-expected New Zealand jobs data, but pushed to new highs in past couple minutes as Aussie sales data weaker than expected. "Feels like we're going to be in a for a really volatile ride here. We could just as easily be in great shape tomorrow though if (US) payrolls is up sharply and ECB says it will do whatever it takes," says Auld. 3-year last up 6 ticks at 94.76, 10-year up 8 ticks at 94.41. (geoffrey.rogow@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0154 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/IDR sharply higher at 9,200 vs 9,115 late yesterday as investors turn risk averse due to concerns over future of nation's economy after Finance Minister Mulyani leaves office. "The dollar, however, was off its high of IDR9,210 on suspected Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," says trader at local bank; tips pair in 9,150-9,250 band for rest of day. (edhi.pranasidhi@dowjones.com) [ 05-05-10 2204ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100506e65600024\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
