\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: Indonesia Shares End Up 0.5%; Bumi Leads\b0\par\par\uc2 1,295 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 April 2010\par 11:18\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global FX & Fixed Income News\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; \par MarketTalk@dowjones.com \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0918 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Indonesia shares end +0.5% at 2900.530 in moderate volume, helped by steady IDR, gains in many Asian markets, traders say; expect shares to consolidate tomorrow after gains in previous 3 sessions; tip index at 2890-2920 range. "Expectations that many companies will announce strong first quarter earnings on firmer rupiah and higher commodity prices kept the main index in positive territory despite sporadic profit taking by local funds," says trader at Kresna Securities ; index ends off intraday high of 2912.467. Among gainers: coal miner Bumi (BUMI.JK) +2.1% at IDR2,450, nickel miner Inco (INCO.JK) +5.1% at IDR5,150, while shipper Berlian Laju (BLTA.JK) +7.6% at IDR710. Profit taking hits gas and oil producer Medco (MEDC.JK) down 2.4% at IDR3,000. (edhi.pranasidhi@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 0917 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] Treasurys inch up in London trading as stocks come off their highs and safe havens get a boost on lingering worries over Greek finances. Thursday brings a raft of data, with NY Fed Empire Survey and jobless claims data, both due at 1230 GMT. Treasury international capital flows figures for February are due 1300 GMT. March industrial production figures are out 1315 GMT and Philadelphia Fed Manufacturing Index survey is out 1400 GMT. Speakers include Dallas Fed's Fisher, \uc2 Richmond Fed\uc2 's Lacker, \uc2 St. Louis Fed\uc2 's Bullard and \uc2 Atlanta Fed\uc2 's Lockhart, who speaks on the economic outlook. The 2-year note is near-flat at 99 30/32 yielding 1.032%, 10-year note up 6+/32 at 98 09/32 to yield 3.836% while 30-year is up 13/32 at 98 22+/32 to yield 4.706%. The June bund contract is up at 123.31 while the June gilt is up 13bps at 114.18. (neelabh.chaturvedi@dowjones.com) Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 Markettalk.eu@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 0917 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] So much for the post-Bernanke EUR/USD bounce. Greek nerves are back in control, and the pair has plunged under $1.3550 from 1.3666 day's peak. (katie.martin@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0917 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] USD/PHP extends losses, sliding to fresh 20-month low late, in line with rise of regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ; pair at 44.31 from 44.50 late Wednesday amid heavy trade; pair's slide tempered by profit-taking, says local bank trader. Adds pair may head further lower Friday as market eyes overseas cues. "We expect some profit-taking tomorrow but the general trend is for the peso to appreciate further." Strong support 44.20, resistance 44.50. (rhea.sandique-carlos@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0916 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] Sterling has sunk straight back down after early gains against the dollar, offering a hint that the $1.5525 area might be a bridge too far right now. USD has also jumped vs EUR as Greek nerves resurface yet again. GBP/USD at day's low of 1.5455. EUR/USD at day's low of 1.3555. (katie.martin@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0915 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] China GDP stronger than expected but imminent tightening is unlikely, says Dong Tao, Credit Suisse 's chief regional economist, non-Japan Asia; has been "a bigger than expected moderation in inflation (while) Beijing said the high growth has been achieved mainly by the base effect and government stimulus. (Also), industrial investment is still missing and the export recovery is strong but remains fragile." Adds one area standing out from an otherwise "Goldilocks situation" is property market, with prices still on rise; expects more tightening measures for sector, and a property market correction in 2H10 or 1H11 "remains the biggest downside risk for China's growth prospects." Says inflation pressure may emerge in 2H10 to trigger a rate hike. (Rosalind.Mathieson@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0914 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] Malaysia's benchmark KLCI turns positive late, ends +0.2% at 1338.83 on bargain buying in blue chips, after stocks trade in negative territory most of day. Construction plays (+0.5%) lead gains on hopes of more jobs after IJM (3336.KU) gets Sarawak contract, but tech stocks (down 0.8%) lower on profit taking after recent gains, says local dealer. OSK Research says keeps near-term bullish outlook, though says market appears to "struggle" around 1338, which represents neckline of modified head and should bearish reversal pattern in 2008; if 1338 breached, 1344-1358 downside gap will form next resistance zone. Support seen at 1334, then 1300. Decliners beat advancers 372 to 269. KNM (7184.KU) ends down 10.2% at MYR0.66 on failed buy out, Top Glove (7113.KU) down 1.1% at MYR12.60, CIMB (1023.KU) down 0.6% at MYR14.08; \uc2 Lafarge\uc2  (3794.KU) closes +4.9% at MYR6.80, IJM +1.9% at MYR4.95, Axiata (6888.KU) +2.4% at MYR3.81. (kwan-por.lee@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0912 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] USD/IDR well supported at 9,000 on suspected \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers say; \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  likely bought total $200 million between 9,000-9,010, helps lift pair from 9,000 intraday low to 9,008 now, but still tad below 9,010 late yesterday. "I think \uc2 Bank Indonesia\uc2  will continue to support the dollar at IDR9,000 Friday to slow down its recent rapid fall so as not to hurt Indonesian exports," a dealer says; 9,000-9,020 range tipped for tomorrow. (i-made.sentana@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0904 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] Data over the last few days has confirmed that the global recovery is continuing apace with inflation pressures remaining subdued. As \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2  says, "global economies are developing within a risk supporting sweet spot, defined by strong economic growth rates combined with low inflation data." (nick.hastings@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0902 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] Bunds tick up as Greek bond yields surge, widening the spread Greece must pay investors to buy its debt instead of safe-haven bunds. There are concerns about possible delays to any aid plan for Greece, with the market also worried about potential debt troubles in other peripheral countries such as Portugal. June bunds are up 13bps at 123.27 and the benchmark 10-year bund is up at 101.11 to yield 3.116%. (neelabh.chaturvedi@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0846 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] Taiwan interbank overnight rate climbs higher to nearly 14-month high 0.165% vs 0.164% yesterday on cash demand from brokerage houses, but rise limited as foreign banks have excess cash on hand, says foreign bank trader. "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't accept (large amount of) NCDs/CDs purchase from foreign banks these days," she says, noting \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has actively drained excess liquidity by accepting more purchase of NCDs/CDs from banks in previous weeks. Tips rate biased up as \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  expected to hike short-term rates gradually in short term. (mason.wu@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0843 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] Sweden's spring budget has an overly optimistic view of overall economic trends and domestic consumption, says Swedbank. Swedbank adds that hopes for declining unemployment could prove to be premature, noting "the government could have stimulated the economy somewhat more last year to limit the downturn." The bank adds that much in the budget had been announced in advance. The yield on Sweden's two-year bond trades one basis point lower at 1.51%, while the 10-year bond yield trades one basis point higher at 3.21%. (karl.bruze@dowjones.com) [ 04-15-10 0518ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100415e64f0006t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
