\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: USD/IDR Well Floored At 9,000; Suspected CB Buys\b0\par\par\uc2 1,206 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 April 2010\par 11:12\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; \par MarketTalk@dowjones.com \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0912 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/IDR well supported at 9,000 on suspected Bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , dealers say; \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  likely bought total $200 million between 9,000-9,010, helps lift pair from 9,000 intraday low to 9,008 now, but still tad below 9,010 late yesterday. "I think Bank Indonesia will continue to support the dollar at IDR9,000 Friday to slow down its recent rapid fall so as not to hurt Indonesian exports," a dealer says; 9,000-9,020 range tipped for tomorrow. (i-made.sentana@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 0904 GMT [Dow Jones] Data over the last few days has confirmed that the global recovery is continuing apace with inflation pressures remaining subdued. As \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2  says, "global economies are developing within a risk supporting sweet spot, defined by strong economic growth rates combined with low inflation data." (nick.hastings@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0902 GMT [Dow Jones] Bunds tick up as Greek bond yields surge, widening the spread Greece must pay investors to buy its debt instead of safe-haven bunds. There are concerns about possible delays to any aid plan for Greece, with the market also worried about potential debt troubles in other peripheral countries such as Portugal. June bunds are up 13bps at 123.27 and the benchmark 10-year bund is up at 101.11 to yield 3.116%. (neelabh.chaturvedi@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0846 GMT [Dow Jones] Taiwan interbank overnight rate climbs higher to nearly 14-month high 0.165% vs 0.164% yesterday on cash demand from brokerage houses, but rise limited as foreign banks have excess cash on hand, says foreign bank trader. "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't accept (large amount of) NCDs/CDs purchase from foreign banks these days," she says, noting \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has actively drained excess liquidity by accepting more purchase of NCDs/CDs from banks in previous weeks. Tips rate biased up as \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  expected to hike short-term rates gradually in short term. (mason.wu@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0843 GMT [Dow Jones] Sweden's spring budget has an overly optimistic view of overall economic trends and domestic consumption, says Swedbank. Swedbank adds that hopes for declining unemployment could prove to be premature, noting "the government could have stimulated the economy somewhat more last year to limit the downturn." The bank adds that much in the budget had been announced in advance. The yield on Sweden's two-year bond trades one basis point lower at 1.51%, while the 10-year bond yield trades one basis point higher at 3.21%. (karl.bruze@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0842 GMT [Dow Jones] Despite recent strong rally, Mandiri Sekuritas still recommends buy on Indonesian government's 20-year FR52 as current 9.89% yield is still higher than fair yield of 9.80%; tips to take profit on 17-year FR45 (yield 10.05%) and 10-year FR31 (yield 8.64%; Offshore investors flocking to Indonesian sovereign bonds lured by relatively high yields, improving economic fundamentals and political stability. (i-made.sentana@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0841 GMT [Dow Jones] The turmoil in Greece continues to keep a bid in the German bond market and "again and again" squeezes short positions in bonds, says \uc2 Danske Bank\uc2 . Adds as long as the Greek situation remains unresolved, it is hard to imagine a strong sell-off [in German paper]. "We do expect the situation to fade away at some point, but admittedly we have been disappointed many times and the timing is uncertain," \uc2 Danske Bank\uc2  says. Adds getting over the May financing hump, with or without help from the European Union and the International Monetary Fund, will be critical. (emese.bartha@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0840 GMT [Dow Jones] China data "all seems rather a Goldilocks outcome, arguing for no urgent change in policy settings, which may well be how top leaders spin it. Certainly there is no 'smoking gun' in the data for near term action on the yuan as a weapon against imported inflation," says \uc2 Westpac\uc2 ; house sticks with call for movement on CNY sometime in 2Q, though adds "it may end up being May-June (post-Strategic Economic Dialogue meetings in Beijing)." Says "a rate hike also does not seem imminent, though as noted earlier in the week the soft March new loans data brought the first quarter total loans to a stunning minus 43% on-year, so a rate rise would seem almost redundant."(Rosalind.Mathieson@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0839 GMT [Dow Jones] Polish zloty is slightly weaker amid uncertainty over future leadership of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and potential \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Bank Pekao says. Adds that 3.85 to the euro, the level at which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  recently \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gains remains crucial. "Gains below 3.85 would open the way towards 3.83, while a move above 3.86-3.87 would limit appreciation potential," the note said. Now EUR/PLN at 3.8615 from 3.8590 Wed; USD/PLN at 2.8445 from 2.8325. (marek.strzelecki@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0837 GMT [Dow Jones] Greece 5-year CDS is moving wider again Thursday, with spreads around 8bps wider on the day at 441bps, according to CMA DataVision. "It looks pretty clear now that the EU/IMF bail out package for Greece has failed to reassure investors on the longer term sustainability of Greece's fiscal position," says \uc2 Evolution Securities\uc2 . Peripheral peer Portugal is also under pressure after the EC published its assessment of the country's growth and stability programme, "concluding that the current crisis impact on Portuguese public finances is severe," says Evolution. Portugal's 5-year CDS spreads are around 14bps wider on the day at 192bps, data from CMA shows. (clare.conanghan@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0825 GMT [Dow Jones] The DMO auctions GBP0.9 billion of UKT 0.625% 2042 linkers and according to \uc2 Barclays Capital\uc2 , the auction should go well. The 30-year sector appears the least rich on the real yield curve and the 2042 linker offers attractive relative value having cheapened notably versus its peers, \uc2 Barclays\uc2  says, adding that the auction will be aided by an overhang of fiscal year-end allocations. (neelabh.chaturvedi@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 0823 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/TWD falls to near 20-month low 31.375 late vs 31.460 late, marking 10th session of declines so far in 13 sessions, with \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  suspected of letting pair fall sharply in 2 sessions, as "the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't want the New Taiwan dollar to be the target of speculators, which will likely to happen if the New Taiwan dollar didn't follow the regional rising trend," says local bank trader. Still, expects \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to start to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  market actively in following session, as TWD has risen much these days. Tips pair in 31.300-31.420 band Friday. Pair weighed by foreign fund inflows, Taiex 0.9% gains, with foreign investors net buyers of NT$9.71 billion Taiwan shares today, marking 14th straight session of net buying. (mason.wu@dowjones.com) [ 04-15-10 0512ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100415e64f0006l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
