\par\par \b \uc2 *DJ Indonesia Unlikely To Limit Foreign Ownership Of Notes -  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Official\b0\par\par\uc2 542 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 April 2010\par 11:54\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2010, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 7 Apr 2010 05:55 EDT *DJ  Indonesia To Boost Corporate Bond Market To Tap Inflows - Central Banker\par \par \uc2 7 Apr 2010 05:55 EDT *DJ  Bank Indonesia Not Worried By Rupiah Level - Central Banker\par \par \uc2 7 Apr 2010 05:55 EDT *DJ  Indonesia Inflation Doesn't Warrant Rate Hikes Yet - Central Banker\par \par \uc2 7 Apr 2010 05:56 EDT *DJ  Indonesia \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Official Was Speaking To Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 7 Apr 2010 05:56 EDT =DJ  INTERVIEW: Indonesia Unlikely To Limit Foreign Ownership Of Notes\par \par \uc2 By David Roman\par \par \uc2 Of Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 NHA TRANG, Vietnam (Dow Jones)--Indonesia is unlikely to set limits on the foreign ownership of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  notes, and will instead boost the development of its corporate bond market to absorb surging fund inflows, a deputy governor of Bank Indonesia said Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has decided against imposing these limits on SBI notes, short-term instruments paying high interest rates that are used to soak up liquidity, following a recent study that found such measures would have negative effects on an economy that is still very much dependent on foreign financing, said Hartadi Sarwono.\par \par \uc2 He was speaking to Dow Jones Newswires on the sidelines of a meeting of top officials from the Association of Southeast Asian Nations.\par \par \uc2 "There is no problem with inflows, as long as we utilize them for the development of our domestic economy," he said.\par \par \uc2 Sarwono's comments follow recent speculation that Bank Indonesia was planning to curtail foreign ownership of SBIs at a time when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is forced to step up expensive issuance to remove liquidity, given strong inflows into the country. Foreigners now own about 20% of SBIs, Sarwono said, the highest proportion ever, as Indonesia has become a preferred destination for global investors lured by economic growth rates that may approach double digits this year.\par \par \uc2 This has pushed the Indonesian rupiah to its highest level against the U.S. dollar since early 2008, despite continued Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets that has resulted in a buildup of foreign reserves, currently at all-time high levels.\par \par \uc2 Sarwono said that Bank Indonesia believes the rupiah's current exchange rate is not a matter for concern, but further strength may erode the competitiveness of the country's exporters, especially if the gains are quick. He said there's a level for the dollar-rupiah rate that the bank considers dangerous for the economy, but he declined to provide a specific figure.\par \par \uc2 He said that Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  plans to keep \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to smooth out volatility, but it isn't looking to reverse trends.\par \par \uc2 On policy rates, Sarwono called current inflation levels "benign" and said they don't warrant a rate increase for the moment, but Bank Indonesia will keep a close eye on any inflation uptick, especially if the government goes ahead with plans to raise electricity and oil tariffs in the second half.\par \par \uc2 "The important thing for the market is to look at the inflation outlook," he added.\par \par \uc2 -By David Roman, Dow Jones Newswires, 65 9455 2447, david.roman@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 April 07, 2010 05:56 ET (09:56 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020100407e64700267\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
