\par\par \b \uc2 *DJ Bank Indonesia Official: Year-End Inflation Likely 4.8%\b0\par\par\uc2 330 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 April 2010\par 08:02\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2010, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 6 Apr 2010 02:05 EDT *DJ  Bank Indonesia Official: Won't Hike Rates If Not 'Really Necessary'\par \par \uc2 6 Apr 2010 02:08 EDT *DJ  Bank Indonesia: Not Targeting Certain Rupiah Level Against Dollar\par \par \uc2 6 Apr 2010 02:09 EDT *DJ  Bank Indonesia: Rupiah's Current Rise Due To Global Developments\par \par \uc2 6 Apr 2010 02:10 EDT *DJ  Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 : Ready To \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  In \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Market If Necessary\par \par \uc2 6 Apr 2010 02:42 EDT DJ  Bank Indonesia Official: Rate Hike Only If "Really Necessary"\par \par \uc2 JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--Bank Indonesia's acting governor reiterated that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  won't increase rates in the next few months unless it's "really necessary."\par \par \uc2 Darmin Nasution, who made the comment after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  decided Tuesday to keep its key rate unchanged at 6.5%, said inflation will likely reach 4.8% by year-end if the government doesn't raise administered energy prices.\par \par \uc2 Most recently, Indonesia's annual inflation eased to 3.43% in March from 3.81% in February due to lower basic food prices.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Bank Indonesia predicted that the economy will grow 5.5%-6% this year, after expanding 4.5% last year.\par \par \uc2 The rupiah on Tuesday rose to its highest level against the dollar since August 2008, which Nasution attributed to global developments. He said Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  was ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market if necessary to stop the rupiah's rise but that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't have a specific target level for the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as "the costs to set a certain level will be expensive."\par \par \uc2 Those remarks suggest Bank Indonesia may allow the rupiah to appreciate further, albeit gradually.\par \par \uc2 High-yield seekers have been buying Indonesian assets thanks to its improving economic fundamentals.\par \par \uc2 -By Farida Husna and Joko Hariyanto; Dow Jones Newswires; 62-21 39831277; I-Made.Sentana@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 April 06, 2010 02:42 ET (06:42 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020100406e646000qh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
