\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: USD/IDR Off 20-Mo Low On Suspected  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 1,195 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 April 2010\par 11:13\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; \par MarketTalk@dowjones.com \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0913 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/IDR at 9,050 vs 9,065 late yesterday, off 20-month low of 9,035 on suspected Bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , dealers say; \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  suspected to have bought around $400 million between 9,035-9,045 to slow pair's slide; \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  wouldn't comment on specific \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but acting governor Nasution says today \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ready to act in market if necessary; it's occasionally spotted buying greenback in recent months after pair fell below 9,400; dealers tip 9,035-9,060 range Wednesday. (i-made.sentana@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 0908 GMT [Dow Jones] Taiwan's inflationary pressure, while gradually rising, remains moderate, meaning \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will keep benchmark interest rate at record low of 1.25% at least through 3Q, says Chinatrust Commercial Bank economist Alan Liao. Taiwan CPI +1.27% in March on year, marking 3rd straight month of increase but slowing down from +2.35% in February, while WPI +6.61% as global commodities prices rose while TWD remained subdued vs USD. "But (domestic) demand remains moderate so there's likely no chance of a demand push that will cause the wholesale prices to filter into consumer prices," says Liao, expects \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to continue monitoring inflation, unemployment, tips 25 bps hike in September. (alex.pevzner@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0904 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/MYR down at 3.2100 late, 21-month low, but off intraday low of 3.2060, vs yesterday's 3.2260; dealer with local bank-backed brokerage says pair continues to trend lower with sellers of dollar active in market after Easter break. No sign of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , means "smooth downward slide for the pair," says dealer. Adds, many brokers looking at revising targets for USD/MYR, some as low as 3.1000, on expectations Asia could outpace Europe, U.S. in economic recovery. "We expect the ringgit to continue to rise in the short term but there could be intermittent profit taking," dealer adds. Tips 3.2000-3.2200 range. (kwan-por.lee@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0903 GMT [Dow Jones] Taiwan average interbank overnight rate unchanged at 0.150%, as \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  seems to have slowed down pace of draining excess funds recently, judging from fewer sales of short-term paper (NCDs/CDs) Thursday, Friday, says local bank trader. "The rising pace of the overnight rate will not be as fast as recent weeks, unless the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  decides to drain excess funds actively" by selling larger-than-expected amounts of NCDs/CDs in short term, he says. Taiwan average interbank overnight rate rose to 14-month high 0.163% last week. (mason.wu@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0858 GMT [Dow Jones] Hungarian forint is unchanged at 264.80 against the EUR in lackluster trade. Investors are reluctant to open new positions ahead of the upcoming parliamentary elections Sunday, \uc2 Commerzbank\uc2  says. Hungary's ability to maintain its commitment to prudent fiscal policy will remain investors' main concern, it adds. As the cross was unable last week to break the 265-267 range seen at end-February and early March, the HUF will continue to seek direction, Raiffeisen Bank says. (margit.feher@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0856 GMT [Dow Jones] India government bonds slip tad from highs as market remains cautious ahead of fresh supply later this week, says trader with foreign bank; 6.35% 2020 bond at 90.23 vs 90.33 session high, 90.20 at Monday's close. "Until new supply hits the market, yields are not going to rise," says trader. Adds, onset of fresh supply may spark spike in yields as market grapples with absorbing government's borrowing programme. Tips yields on 10-year benchmark bond to test 8% next week. RBI will auction bonds of INR120 billion Friday.(khushita.vasant@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0851 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/PHP lower late, under pressure from substantial inflows from overseas Filipino workers following Easter break; pair at 44.92, lowest since August 2008, from 45.01 late Monday. "This is still part of the inflows that we accumulated over the weekend," says local bank trader. Tips pair may head towards 45.15 resistance Wednesday, adding "market has been pretty oversold," citing substantial peso gains in recent sessions. Next support 44.80. (rhea.sandique-carlos@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0843 GMT [Dow Jones] The rise in the annual rate of Swiss March inflation shows the strong CHF hasn't been able to damp imported price increases, says Vontobel. As expected, the Swiss CPI rose an annual 1.4%, largely driven by a 17% rise in energy and fuel costs, says economist Ralf Wiedenmann. (neil.maclucas@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0840 GMT [Dow Jones] \uc2 UBS\uc2  recommends a short EUR/GBP position, expressed through options, as GBP has stabilized of late, and the expected announcement of the UK election date later Tuesday should remove some uncertainty on the UK front. "Paradoxically, the beginning of the election campaign may prove GBP positive," bank says. Meanwhile, sovereign debt concerns continue to weigh on EUR. Cross now trades at 0.8839 with GBP under broad pressure. (katie.martin@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0838 GMT [Dow Jones] Price pressures in Switzerland remain moderate despite a quickening of consumer-price inflation in March, according to \uc2 Credit Suisse\uc2 . "However, given the increasing signs of a broad-based economic recovery and the \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2 's longer-term outlook for an inflation rate above the target band, we assume it will move to a less expansionary monetary policy in the months ahead," says CS economist Fabian Heller. (neil.maclucas@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0823 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/TWD falls to 19-month low 31.695 late vs 31.759 yesterday, but off intraday low 31.651 as \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  suspected of buying USD to slow pair's drop, 2 traders at local banks say. Both traders estimate \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have bought over US$100 million Tuesday. "The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  today is quite mild...(which means) the pair is likely to test next key support at 31.500 near term," says local bank trader, noting pair ended below key 31.700 mark in Taipei first time since Sep. 1 2008, level \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  suspected of firmly defending in past months. Pair weighed by foreign fund inflows as foreign investors buy net NT$18.62 billion Taiwan shares Tuesday. Tips pair in 31.630-31.700 band Wednesday. (mason.wu@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0823 GMT [Dow Jones] The acceleration in March Swiss inflation reflects higher energy costs and isn't material on the medium-term monetary policy horizon, says ING. "As elsewhere in Europe, Swiss inflation is set to show some months of rates above 1%, but this should not last for long," says analyst Julien Manceaux. "We still believe the first \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2  rate hike will take place this year, but too strong a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  might alter this call," he notes. EUR/CHF was last at 1.43177 from a high of 1.4327. (neil.maclucas@dowjones.com) [ 04-06-10 0513ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100406e64600066\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
