\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Won dips on dlr strength; rupiah  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  seen\b0\par\par\uc2 681 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Februar 2010\par 07:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Won loses 1 percent, Goldman expects firmer won over time\par \par \uc2 * Indonesian c.bank seen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support rupiah\par \par \uc2 * Most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  shackled in tight ranges\par \par \uc2 By Kevin Yao\par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, Feb 25 (Reuters) - The South Korean won fell 1 percent on Thursday, tracking the euro's weakness amid lingering investor concerns over debt problems in Europe, while the rupiah's decline again sparked official \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  mostly moved in thin ranges as sentiment was torn between the Fed's affirmation on low rates and persistent jitters over fiscal woes in Europe.\par \par \uc2 The euro slid to a one-year low of 120.60 yen <EURJPY=> and fell below $1.3470 <EUR=>, hurt by persistent worries about Greece's fiscal woes. [ID:nTOE61O03X]\par \par \uc2 Worries about a possible downgrade of Greece weighed. \uc2 Standard & Poor's\uc2  saying on Wednesday it may cut Greece's BBB+ rating by one or two notches within a month. [ID:nLDE61N2KL]\par \par \uc2 WON\par \par \uc2 The won <KRW=> shed nearly 1 percent to 1,164.6 per dollar, its lowest in two weeks.\par \par \uc2 The won has lost almost 4 percent since early January due to the dollar's resurgence and a sell-off of risky assets fanned by worries about European debt problems.\par \par \uc2 The won may be pressured in the near-term by South Korea's worsening balance of payments due to pent-up oil demand and other factors that led to a current account deficit in January, analysts at \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 South Korea reported the biggest monthly exports decline in January in a year, pushing the current account balance into deficit and providing new evidence that the economic revival is losing steam. [ID:nTOE61N090]\par \par \uc2 "Beyond the near term, the won is still supported by a positive outlook for capital inflows and ship and construction orders," Goldman analysts noted.\par \par \uc2 The bank kept its won forecasts at 1,150, 1,100 and 1,050 over 3, 6, and 12-month horizons, respectively.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, official dollar/won non-deliverable forwards <KRWNDFOR=> rose, tracking the weaker euro.\par \par \uc2 "One-month NDFs opened at 1,152.0 and then went as high as 1,159 when euro dropped below $1.35," said a trader in Singapore.\par \par \uc2 RUPIAH\par \par \uc2 The rupiah <IDR=> lost as much as 0.6 percent to 9,360 but later stabilised near 9,350 as traders suspected dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "The rupiah hit 9,360 before BI came in," said a trader in Jakarta.\par \par \uc2 A second trader said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was providing dollar liquidity to meet corporate demand for monthly settlements.\par \par \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  many times in recent weeks to support the high-yielding rupiah, which is vulnerable to risk aversion. It has lost more than 2 percent since early January. \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day at  0634 GMT\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        89.47          90.20       +0.82\par  Sing dlr        1.4115         1.4100       -0.11\par  Taiwan dlr      32.093         32.090       -