\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Won, rupiah dip after Fed lifts discount rate\b0\par\par\uc2 694 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Februar 2010\par 04:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Won's implied vols edge up as spot slips\par \par \uc2 * Indonesian c.bank seen smoothing rupiah's fall\par \par \uc2 * Dollar/peso NDFs rise but lack momentum\par \par \uc2 By Kevin Yao\par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, Feb 19 (Reuters) - The South Korean won led Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  lower on Friday as the Federal Reserve's surprise discount rate rise spurred a dollar rally, prompting Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the second day.\par \par \uc2 The dollar hit a 8-month high against major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  <.DXY> after the Federal Reserve said it would raise the discount rate to 0.75 percent from 0.50 percent, stoking expectations that it is moving towards normalising policy. [ID:nTOE61I03G]\par \par \uc2 Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have been undermined in recent weeks by the dollar's broad resurgence and capital outflows associated with the sell-off in riskier assets, and higher U.S. interest rates tend to encourage such outflows.\par \par \uc2 Markets in China and Taiwan remained shut for holidays.\par \par \uc2 WON\par \par \uc2 The won <KRW=> lost as much as 0.9 percent to 1,161.20 per dollar, but it later stabilised near 1,160.\par \par \uc2 Implied volatilities in the won <KRWVOL> edged up as the spot slipped, but investors appeared to be reluctant to snap up volatilities amid signs that the won was stabilising.\par \par \uc2 "We just see a bit of buying interest in the front-end with dollar/won spot moving higher," said an option trader in Singapore.\par \par \uc2 One-month vols rose to 12.64 percent from 12.49 percent late on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The vols hit as high as 16.6 percent earlier this month as the won's steep decline caught investors off guard, but they have come off steadily as the spot rate recovered.\par \par \uc2 RUPIAH\par \par \uc2 The rupiah <IDR=> fell as much as 0.8 percent to 9,365 to the dollar, but it later cut losses as traders suspected dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  started selling dollars from 9,350 to 9,365," said a trader in Jakarta, adding that the rupiah could quickly fall to 9,400 if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 A second trader said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was aiming to check the rupiah's volatility amid broad dollar strength in recent sessions.\par \par \uc2 PESO\par \par \uc2 Dollar/peso non-deliverable forwards jumped across the curve in line with the dollar's broad rally, but the rise lacked momentum, traders said.\par \par \uc2 "We see higher bids at the opening but not much now," said a NDF trader in Manila.\par \par \uc2 One-month NDFs <PHP1MNDFOR=> hit as high 46.51 in early trade compared to 46.25 late on Thursday, while onshore forwards with the same tenor <PHP1M=> edged up to 46.42 from Thursday's 45.26.\par \par \uc2 That means offshore markets price in a bit more peso depreciation compared to onshore.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, spot peso <PHP=> fell 0.4 percent to 46.39 per dollar but traders expected it to get near-term support at 46.40. \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day at   0652 GMT\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        91.90          91.22     