\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: Indonesia Shares End Down 0.2% But Off Lows\b0\par\par\uc2 1,257 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Februar 2010\par 10:25\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; \par MarketTalk@dowjones.com \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0925 GMT [Dow Jones] Indonesia shares end down 0.2% at 2554.376 in light volume, on foreign selling in most blue chips due to weakness of U.S. stocks futures, but index off intraday low of 2528.695; "mild buying by local institutional funds helped lift the main index from its low," says trader at Valbury Securities; expects shares to rebound Monday on bargain buying; tips resistance at 2590. Among decliners: heavyweight Telkom (TLKM.JK) down 1.2% at IDR8,600, off intraday low of IDR8,500, coal miner Bumi (BUMI.JK) down 1.1% at IDR2,300, rebounding from IDR2,250 low. Bucking trend, car distributor Astra (ASII.JK) up 0.4% at IDR36,150, off intraday low of IDR35,500. (EDH)\f28 \par \par \uc2 0918 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/JPY cleared 92.00 overnight and a break above its 200 DMA at 92.27 would clear the way for a restest of the 93.78 January 2010 highs, says \uc2 Lloyds Banking Group\uc2 . USD/JPY now trades at 91.74 from the day's 5-week high of 92.10. (GST)\par \par \uc2 0916 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/IDR up late but off highs, last at 9,348 vs 9,320 late Thursday; off 9,365 peak hit in morning session as suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  caps gains. Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  thought to sell $25 million-$50 million at IDR9,350-IDR9,360 after USD rises on Fed's 25 bps discount rate hike. Market doesn't expect Bank Indonesia will follow suit with early rate hike, dealers say; tip USD/IDR to return to listless, rangebound trading of recent weeks Monday, taking cues from euro, other external factors amid lack of domestic cues; 9,330-9,360 range eyed. (RLC)\par \par \uc2 0915 GMT [Dow Jones] Bunds remain lower on the day after euro zone PMIs printed slightly higher than expectations with February manufacturing PMI printing at 54.1 versus 52.6 forecast, services PMI prints slightly lower at 52.0 versus 52.5 forecast and composite PMI edged up to 53.7 versus 53.4 forecast. The March bund futures contract is currently down 0.24 on the day at 122.74, from a 122.58 day low while the 10-year benchmark bund is down 0.19 at 99.84, yielding 3.268%, from a day's high at 3.295%. (NKA)\par \par \uc2 0914 GMT [Dow Jones] Malaysia shares end lower; benchmark KLCI down 0.1% at 1257.67 in sluggish trade with 489 million shares traded. Dealer with local bank-backed brokerage says market sentiment weaker after Fed hikes discount rate, but index stays in tight 1255-1259 band most of day as investors remain on sidelines. "They aren't willing to take aggressive positions ahead of the weekend," dealer says, adding post-Lunar New Year rebound likely short-lived; "it's probably come and gone." Market breadth negative with 448 decliners vs 157 advancers. Genting (3182.KU) ends down 2.8% at MYR6.36, BAT (4162.KU) down 0.8% at MYR41.64, Mudajaya (5085.KU) down 2.5% at MYR5.39, Tanjong (2267.KU) down 2.2% at MYR17.66. DiGi.Com (6947.KU) finishes +2.3% at MYR22.34, Dutch Lday (3026.KU) +1.7% at MYR12.00. (KPL)\par \par \uc2 0914 GMT [Dow Jones] GBP/USD has lost 3 cents in the last 48 hours as the bulls run for cover notes \uc2 Lloyds Banking Group\uc2 . A weak retail sales report at 0930 GMT could spark the next leg lower with key support seen at 1.5352, although 1.50 looks achievable over coming weeks says the bank. The market consensus for January's weather-hit retail sales is a 0.5% decline although some analysts are looking for a drop of 1%. (GST)\par \par \uc2 0911 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/PHP higher late, in step with USD strength across board following Fed's decision to hike discount rate on banks' emergency loans; pair at 46.28 from 46.20 late Thursday amid heavy trading. "Market expectation of a start of tightening cycle in the U.S. isn't very friendly to the peso," says local bank trader, adding USD advance tempered by most bank's long USD positions. Tips pair may continue to advance, next support 46.20, resistance 46.40.(RSA)\par \par \uc2 0910 GMT [Dow Jones] Depositary receipt fund-raisings by Asia-Pacific companies dominate DR issuances so far this year, with US$303 million raised since start 2010, continuing last year's strong momentum. Asian companies raised US$8.7 billion from DR offerings or 27% of global volume, led by issuances by Chinese, Indian firms. BNY Mellon expects continued interest from U.S. funds, despite increasing number of funds setting up shop in Asia, allowing them to trade Asian stocks real-time. "A very large number of new funds are coming into the market, or funds that were historically locally focused in the U.S. are beginning to look outside the U.S., and they are focusing on depositary receipts because of the convenience," BNY Mellon's Asia-Pacific head of its depositary receipts division Chris Kearn says. See "=FOCUS: Depositary Receipts To Stay Popular Among Asian Companies." (AOR)\par \par \uc2 0905 GMT [Dow Jones] The Fed's surprise discount rate hike kept the USD well supported against most majors as investors speculate on when Fed Funds will be increased. Concern over Greece and other euro-zone debtors continues to weigh on the EUR but the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  did get a little help from the latest euro-zone composite PMI which remained steady. The USD is down a little at Y91.75 while the EUR is down at $1.3497. The GBP sank to $1.5397 ahead of data that is expected to show a sharop drop in UK retail sales. (NEH)\par \par \uc2 0903 GMT [Dow Jones] Friday's firmer EU PMI prints are unlikely to discourage the euro bears and induce a pullback much above $1.35 says \uc2 UniCredit\uc2 . Instead, in the wake of Thursday's Fed discount rate hike a break below $1.34 is likely to spark fresh selling pressure to levels even below $1.33. EUR/USD now at 1.3496 after the euro-zone flash composite PMI came in unchanged at 53.7. (GST)\par \par \uc2 0853 GMT [Dow Jones] India government bonds off lows after Prime Minister's Economic Advisory Panel member Govind Rao says rate action by RBI unlikely before April, also government likely to borrow INR4.5 trillion next fiscal year (same as this FY); 6.35% 2020 bond at 89.59 vs 89.50 before comments, 89.74 Thursday's close. "The markets are still not ready to go long on positions. Even a similar amount of government borrowing next fiscal (year) will be a challenge because of higher inflation threat giving lesser room to RBI to keep rates steady," says dealer. Tips 2020 bond to be in 89.45-89.65 in session. (NAC)\par \par \uc2 0851 GMT [Dow Jones] Short sterling, euribor and eurodollar curves all sell off Friday in reaction to the Fed's discount rate hike as traders priced in a greater chance of monetary policy tightening in the months ahead. The June '10/'11 euribor spread climbs 4 bps to +89 bps, the June '10/'11 short sterling spread steepens 5 bps to +120 bps and the June '10/'11 eurodollar spread rises 5 bps to +135 bps. (NKA) [ 02-19-10 0425ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100219e62j0005v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
