\par\par \b \uc2 ASIA LOCAL BONDS-Philippine, Indonesia bond yields edge lower\b0\par\par\uc2 By Saikat Chatterjee   \par \uc2 474 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Februar 2010\par 08:08\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG, Feb 18 (Reuters) - Philippine bond yields softened on Thursday on growing investor expectations that the government would borrow less from the local bond markets in coming months.\par \par \uc2 Manila will price up to 100 billion yen ($1.1 billion) of Samurai bonds next week and, with tax collections also recovering, the supply pipeline is expected to shrink keeping demand for bonds intact. [ID:nSGE61F0CX].\par \par \uc2 Benchmark five-year bonds <PH5YT=RR> were yielding 5.99 percent, a shade softer than the last close and traders said it could fall to between 5.8-5.9 percent in the coming weeks.\par \par \uc2 "Philippines in particular had made very good progress on fiscal consolidation prior to the crisis and we really need to see what the next administration does," Michael Hasenstab, a fund manager at Franklin Templeton who manages $60 billion in assets, told a Reuters chatroom. [ID:nTOE61H01L].\par \par \uc2 The Philippines, one of Asia's most active sovereign debt issuers, faces a budget shortfall of 293 billion pesos ($6.3 billion), or 3.5 percent of GDP, this year.\par \par \uc2 Latest data showed Manila had a record fiscal deficit of 298.5 billion pesos or 3.9 percent of GDP in 2009.[ID:nMNA002626]\par \par \uc2 It raised $1.5 billion from a global bond sale last month, the from Asia this year. It wants to raise a total of $2.5 billion from foreign debt markets this year to partly fund the budget deficit and repay debts.\par \par \uc2 Philippines goes for national elections in May.\par \par \uc2 INDONESIAN BOND YIELDS EASE\par \par \uc2 In \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , bond yields eased after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  but volume was thin ahead of an auction next week.\par \par \uc2 The high-yielding rupiah <IDR=> fell as much as 0.7 percent in early deals before the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was seen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  according to traders. [ID:nSGE61H04W].\par \par \uc2 Ten-year government bonds <ID10YT=RR> were now yielding 9.83 percent, two basis points below from Wednesday's close of 9.85 percent.\par \par \uc2 Foreign investors have continued to swarm to Indonesian bonds this year on top of aggressive buying last year. This month alone they have bought more than 4 trillion rupiah ($87 million) of bonds after buying $2.2 billion last year.\par \par \uc2 Templeton's Hasenstab said he was positive on the outlook for bonds as policymakers have proved very adept at managing the economy during, adding to the credibility of its macro policy.\par \par \uc2 "Clearly, as with any emerging market there are risks and we need to monitor developments closely, but any country that came through 2009 with positive growth deserves a degree of credit." ($1= 46.1 pesos, 9,300 rupiah) (Editing by Jan Dahinten)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-ASIA-BONDS/|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|PHD|IF|SI|Z|SNI|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100218e62i000e9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
