\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: USD/IDR Higher; Bank Indonesia Eyed Selling $100M\b0\par\par\uc2 1,369 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Januar 2010\par 09:21\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; \par MarketTalk@dowjones.com \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0821 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/IDR higher at 9,430 vs 9,350 late Monday on USD firmness vs regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , spurring Bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , dealers say; \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  suspected of selling total $100 million between 9,380-9,400 to slow pair's rise. "The dollar will likely remain well bid tomorrow also because of month-end demand from Indonesian importers," a dealer says; 9,380-9,450 tipped for Wednesday. (IMS)\f28 \par \par \uc2 0818 GMT [Dow Jones] EUR/JPY slumped to a near nine-month low of 126.12 in Asia Tuesday and \uc2 Mizuho Corporate Bank\uc2 's Nicole Elliott looks for more downside ahead. She says moving averages have crossed to bearish and although the cross is very oversold, bearish momentum is now at its strongest since April '09. While keeping an eye out for the authorities she favors small shorts at market, adding at 128.00 with a stop above 128.55, looking for 126.15, 125.75 and 124.35 on the downside. EUR/JPY now at 127.10. (GST)\par \par \uc2 0815 GMT [Dow Jones] The USD had a mixed overnight session while the JPY was whipped about in Asia. After a fairly uneventful US session Monday, the USD and JPY gained strongly in Asia on safety flows amid reports China was putting into place last week's reported lending curbs on certain banks. USD/JPY slumped to a fresh one-month low of 89.53, EUR/JPY a near 9-month low of 126.12 and EUR/USD lost a cent to 1.4071. However, the JPY's gains were just as quickly reversed after S&P cuts Japan's outlook to negative, citing the nations "diminishing economic policy flexibility." EUR/JPY added 150 sen and USD/JPY almost 100 sen although EUR/USD remained capped below 1.41. The other big mover overnight was sterling. The prospects of the UK coming out of recession at 0930 GMT today when 4Q GDP is announced added one cent to GBP/USD and pushed EUR/GBP back below 0.87. For Tuesday UK GDP and German Ifo grab attention but keep an eye on equities, the Nikkei shed 1.7%, China 2.4% and Europe is heading toward a 1% loss, all of which could further damage risk appetite and give the JPY and USD more upside potential. (GST)\par \par \uc2 0814 GMT [Dow Jones] Attention on the Ifo survey out of Germany, at 0900 GMT, should be more intense than usual given the problems in Greece. As \uc2 Commerzbank\uc2  says: "Only if the economy in the euro zone behaves well will it be possible for Greece to raise taxes sufficiently to achieve a consolidation of the national finances. Against this background risks for EUR/USD are likely to be asymmetrical. While weak data are likely to lead to increased concerns and thus losses in EUR/USD, a positive surprise is expected to create only limited momentum." EUR/USD now at 1.4103. (NEH)\par \par \uc2 0813 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/TWD still higher at 32.055 late (highest since December 30 at 32.238) vs 31.970 late yesterday in heavy trade on short covering by foreign banks after sharp decline in Taiwan shares (Taiex ends down 3.5%), says local bank trader. Volume at NT$1.33 billion vs NT$649 million Monday. Still, gains limited by exporters selling to meet month-end settlement. "The rebound would have exceeded NT$0.2 without exporters' selling," he says. Expects pair to edge up near term, taking further cues from local shares. Tips 32.000-32.150 band Wednesday. (CHY)\par \par \uc2 0811 GMT [Dow Jones] Mounting concerns over China policy risks push Singapore shares lower. STI down 2.0% at 2755.70 vs 2772.49 midday (off 1.4%), with market breadth at 13 decliners for every gainer. All FTSE ST sub-indexes negative. If benchmark fails to hold above 2750, next support tipped at 2729 (November minor low). Overall volume more than whole of yesterday's 1.97 billion shares. "I'm concerned that this would be the start of a sustained correction period. We really have to wait and see before attempting to buy anything at this juncture. A lot of the guys looking at technicals say there's room for the STI to go lower," says dealer at foreign brokerage. Top decliners among STI components include Genting Singapore (G13.SG), down 5.8% at S$1.14, Noble Group (N21.SG) off 4.6% at S$2.88, \uc2 SIA Engineering\uc2  (S59.SG), off 4.7% at S$3.42, \uc2 Golden Agri-Resources\uc2  (E5H.SG), off 4.7% at S$0.51. (FKH)\par \par \uc2 0809 GMT [Dow Jones] Naoto Kan would be well advised to have a JPY \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  plan in place, according to \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  Focus by Nicholas Hastings. Chances are the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will once again head higher--this time taking it even above the level it reached late last year, when the threat of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  became a major issue. (NEH)\par \par \uc2 0754 GMT [Dow Jones] \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 , JGB players say that while surprise S&P cut to Japan outlook moved market, its effect likely to be fleeting and bigger focus is on developments in global share markets; continued weakness in shares would likely spark more risk aversion, possibly pushing JPY back up at expense of risk-sensitive \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  such as EUR and AUD. "S&P's decision was surprising, big news, but I don't think this the main theme in the market. Players are watching the development of share markets," and whether any falls in stocks dent overall market sentiment, says Mitsubishi UFJ Trust and Banking Corp. chief manager Hideaki Inoue. Tips USD/JPY resistance at 90.60, compared with current 90.12. In after-hours trading, JGBs shed earlier gains after S&P announcement, falling 0.10 compared with Tokyo close of 139.28, but one trader says selling represents position adjustment after gains today on weak Nikkei. (MIN, KDM)\par \par \uc2 0753 GMT [Dow Jones] The rand is softer early, largely in line with a weaker euro and ahead of a local interest rate decision. USD/ZAR at 7.6380 from a close of 7.5584. ZAR is expected to continue tracking major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  ahead of the MPC announcement due after 1300 GMT, with the cross looking at a range of 7.58-7.66, a trader says. Economists widely expect the repo to be held at 7%. (I-Net Bridge)\par \par \uc2 0752 GMT [Dow Jones] S&P's revision of Japan's ratings outlook to negative impacting CDS in rest of Asia, say market participants. Markit iTraxx Asia ex-Japan's investment-grade CDS index widens another 5 bps from this morning to 111-116 bps. "The market is becoming overall defensive" after S&P's action, says Brayan Lai, a credit analyst at Calyon in Hong Kong. "It's not a good time. It might slow down the supply pipeline in the meantime," he says. (DLZ)\par \par \uc2 0752 GMT [Dow Jones] March bunds are rising towards resistance at 123.49. A break through here will leave 123.66/123.72 and the last barrier on the way to the 124.06 November high, says \uc2 Societe Generale\uc2  technical analysts. Beyond here lies the medium-term rising resistance line, currently at 124.77. Any weakness should be held up by support at 122.58 and 122.29. The contract trades at 123.39 with resistance standing at 123.49, 123.66/123.72 and 124.06 while support lies at 122.58, 122.29 and 122.02. (NKA)\par \par \uc2 0752 GMT [Dow Jones] Hungarian forint weakens on souring global market mood and not on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's interest rate cut, which had been fully priced in and was, at 25bps, as expected, a dealer says. EUR/HUF is at 273.1 vs 272.1 Monday afternoon. The next support level for HUF is seen around 275 and then at 278, with the lower end of the technical trading range, should HUF firm against the euro, at 266.20, the trader adds. (MAF) [ 01-26-10 0321ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100126e61q0004z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
