\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Ringgit, peso near 16-mth highs on dlr woes, China\b0\par\par\uc2 871 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Januar 2010\par 06:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Dollar slide after poor jobs data spurs Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Ringgit jumps over 1 pct, breaks key resistance at 3.35\par \par \uc2 * Peso gains 0.7 pct to highest since Aug. 2008\par \par \uc2 * Rupiah's rise sparks official \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Yuan NDFs imply faster yuan rise after trade data\par \par \uc2 By Kevin Yao\par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, Jan 11 (Reuters) - The Malaysian ringgit and Philippine peso hit their highest levels in almost 16 months on Monday as the dollar faltered and Chinese data raised hopes of yuan gains, while \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to slow the rise in the rupiah.\par \par \uc2 Asian stocks hit a 17-month high as a strong rebound in China's exports raised optimism about the region's economic outlook, while the dollar suffered its biggest fall in six weeks in the wake of disappointing U.S. jobs data. [ID:nTOE60A009] [IDnSGE60A03L]\par \par \uc2 RINGGIT\par \par \uc2 One-month dollar/ringgit non-deliverable forwards <MYRNDFOR=> slid to 3.3320, the lowest since Aug. 2008 and largely at par with the spot, as offshore investors scrambled to shed long dollar positions.\par \par \uc2 "The market was caught long (on USD) from last Friday," said a Singapore-based dealer.\par \par \uc2 The spot ringgit <MYR=> jumped as much as 1.3 percent to 3.3325, breaking key resistance at 3.35.\par \par \uc2 "Investors are squaring their cross/ringgit positions and so far we see only hedging flows on cross/ringgit here," said a trader in Kuala Lumpur.\par \par \uc2 PESO\par \par \uc2 The peso <PHP=> gained 0.7 percent at 45.48, its highest in nearly 16 months.\par \par \uc2 "The peso is gaining ground on the strong Chinese trade data. It's likely that successive positive data should have China moving towards strengthening the yuan, and the regionals should follow," said a dealer in Manila.\par \par \uc2 Traders say the peso was being driven more by fund inflows by institutions as the wave of remittance inflows seen in Dec. has passed.\par \par \uc2 One-month dollar/peso NDFs <PHP1MNDFOR=> fell from Friday's close of 45.78 to to 45.65, lowst since Aug. 2008.\par \par \uc2 RUPIAH\par \par \uc2 Despite suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the high-yielding rupiah <IDR=> jumped 1 percent to 9,120 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 "BI (the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) does not want the rupiah to move too fast," said a trader in Jakarta.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has gained 3.3 percent against the dollar so far this month, making it the second best preformer among the nine regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  tracked by Reuters.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Indonesian bond yields dropped on falling dollar/rupiah and upbeat comments by PIMCO, the world's biggest fund manager.\par \par \uc2 Chia-Liang Lian, a fund manager at Pacific investment Management Co, said Indonesian local debt was attractive due to its yield appeal versus other markets. [ID:nTOE60A01T].\par \par \uc2 YUAN\par \par \uc2 The benchmark offshore one-year NDFs <CNY1YNDFOR=> fell sharply to a two-month low, implying more yuan appreciation in 12 months after China posted strong foreign trade data over the weekend.\par \par \uc2 The NDFs hit 6.585, down from Friday's close of 6.607, its lowest level since Nov. 13.\par \par \uc2 Twelve-month yuan appreciation implied by NDFs rose to 3.70 percent measured from the Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's daily mid-point, compared with 3.34 percent implied at Friday's close.\par \par \uc2 Expectations that Beijing may unshackle the yuan from a dollar peg gained steam after China's data showed exports leapt 17.7 percent from a year earlier, dwarfing the 4.0 percent rise forecast by economists and breaking a 13-month streak of year-on-year declines. [ID:nSGE60A016]\par \par \uc2 "We bring forward our forecast timing of a PBOC widening of the dollar/yuan trading band to +/- 3 percent from the current +/-0.5 percent from the third quarter of 2010 to the second quarter," analysts at ING said in a note. \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day at   0520 GMT\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen*       92.26          92.61       +0.38\par  Sing dlr        1.3872         1.3945       +0.53\par  Taiwan dlr      31.720         31.880       +0.50\par  Korean won     1118.20        1130.50       +1.10\par  Baht             33.04          33.15       +0.33\par  Peso             45.51          45.81       +0.66\par  Rupiah         9120.00        9210.00       +0.99\par  Rupee            45.36          45.75       +0.86\par  Ringgit         3.3350         3.3750       +1.20\par  Yuan            6.8262         6.8275       +0.02\par  (Japanese financial markets were closed on Monday for a\par holiday)\par  Change so far in 2010\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        92.26          92.90       +0.69\par  Sing dlr        1.3872         1.4053       +1.30\par  Taiwan dlr      31.720         32.030       +0.98\par  Korean won     1118.20        1164.50       +4.14\par  Baht             33.04          33.32       +0.85\par  Peso             45.51          46.20       +1.52\par  Rupiah         9120.00        9420.00