\par\par \b \uc2 Dow Jones Asia-Pacific Top Stories Sked For January 7\b0\par\par\uc2 1,730 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Januar 2010\par 08:03\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Following are the top Asia-Pacific stories featured on Dow Jones Newswires as of 0700 GMT. Not all stories appear on all wires. Please direct any questions or comments toasianewseds@dowjones.com.\par \par \uc2 MACRO/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /FIXED INCOME:\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: PBOC RAISES KEY BILL YIELD, SIGNALS POLICY SHIFT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  unexpectedly raised a key interbank market interest rate Thursday for the first time in nearly five months, signaling a change in its policy focus toward pre-empting inflation risks in the new year. (published 0610 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: KOREA PRESSURES \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TO KEEP RATES LOW \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's government said Thursday it will start sitting in on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy meetings, an unexpected step that will pressure the Bank of Korea to keep interest rates low. (published 0633 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =2ND UPDATE:PHILIPPINES PAYS ONLY SMALL PREMIUM IN $1.5B BOND SALE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Philippines had to pay only a small premium over yields of its existing global bonds as investors leapt at its $1.5 billion offering overnight, helping contain its borrowing costs despite a record-wide budget deficit and underlining investor hunger for new issues out of Asia. (published 0516 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: AUSTRALIAN NOVEMBER RETAIL SALES STRONG; RBA FEBRUARY HIKE IN FOCUS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australian retail sales surged in November rising at the fastest pace since economic stimulus gushed into the economy at the start of 2009, stoking the case for the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of Australia\f28 \uc2 \f2  to raise interest rates at its next policy meeting in early February. (published 0504 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =2ND UPDATE:NEW ZEALAND TRADE DEFICIT SHRINKS AS IMPORTS SLUMP \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New Zealand's trade deficit shrank in November and was smaller than expected, helping lift the New Zealand dollar to a seven-week high. But a slump in imports that led to the smaller shortfall is unlikely to persist, as New Zealand's anemic economy gradually regains strength. (published 0257 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par NATIONAL PENSION SERVICE TO BUY AROUND $400 MLN THURSDAY IN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCY\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MARKET - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's \f28 \uc2 \f2 National Pension Service\f28 \uc2 \f2  is likely to buy around $400 million in the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market Thursday after purchasing more than that amount a day earlier, a person familiar with the matter said Thursday. (published 0153 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =DJ DATA SNAP: INDIA PRIMARY ARTICLES PRICE INDEX +14.39% IN WEEK TO DEC 26 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's primary articles price index rose 14.39% from a year earlier to 282.2 in the week to Dec. 26, shows data issued by the Ministry of Commerce and Industry Thursday. (published 0653 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par S KOREA NOVEMBER M1 MONEY SUPPLY GROWTH SLOWEST IN SIX MONTHS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's short-term funds grew at the slowest pace in six months in November, easing from a seven-year high the previous month, according to Bank of Korea data issued Thursday. (published 0300 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SOUTH KOREA BANKS' 2009 AVERAGE DAILY \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TRADE FALLS 8.3% TO $21.19 BLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The average daily volume of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  trading among South Korean banks fell 8.3% to $21.19 billion last year as increased volatility led to cautious trading, especially in the first four months, the Bank of Korea said Thursday. (published 0300 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AUCKLAND DEC HOMES SALES DOWN 25% FROM NOV, UP 40.6% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Home sales in New Zealand's commercial capital Auckland fell 25% in December from November, but were up 40.6% from a year earlier, a report from a real estate company released Thursday showed. (published 0026 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BANK INDONESIA OFFICIAL: RUPIAH'S RECENT RISE "QUITE FAST" \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The rupiah's recent appreciation has been "quite fast", but it is likely temporary, Bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said Thursday after reportedly \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in favor of the dollar earlier in the day. (published 0525 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ASIA: INTERBANK RATE TREND SUGGESTS DOLLAR TO RISE VS YEN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The end of a long period of yen strength is likely here, brought on by expectations that U.S. and Japanese monetary policies - and the interbank lending rates that play off of policy rates - may soon diverge. (published 0453 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 EQUITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: SAMSUNG ESTIMATES IT SWUNG TO 4Q PROFIT, RECORD HIGH SALES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Samsung Electronics Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., the world's biggest maker of memory chips and flat-screen TVs, said Thursday it expects to report that it swung to an operating profit for the fourth quarter over the year-earlier period, with sales likely rising to a record high. (published 0636 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BANK-LED JAL REFORM PLAN INCLUDES SHAREHOLDER OWNERSHIP REDUCTION -SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank creditors of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Japan Airlines Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . have proposed a turnaround plan that includes a request for its shareholders to accept a reduction in their ownership stakes and over Y300 billion in debt forgiveness, including debt-for-equity swaps, a person familiar with the matter said Thursday. (published 0649 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: \f28 \uc2 \f2 LG ELECTRONICS\f28 \uc2 \f2  SEES GLOBAL SALES UP 10% THIS YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 LG Electronics Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Thursday it aims to increase global sales by around 10% this year to KRW59 trillion as the South Korean consumer electronics maker moves to boost revenue from new businesses such as solar cells. (published 0617 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: CHINA NATIONAL CHEMICAL ENGINEERING MAKES WEAK DEBUT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China National Chemical Engineering Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . made a subdued trading debut Thursday in the country's first main board listing of the new year, extending the trend of new listings in recent months as an increase in the number of initial public offerings and their high valuations hit demand. (published 0401 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: FORD'S 2009 CHINA SALES FROM JVS, IMPORTS JUMP 44% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Ford Motor Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Thursday sales in China last year from its local joint ventures and imports rose 44% to a record 440,619 units, in sharp contrast to the U.S. carmaker's decline in sales at home. (published 0526 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: MICROSOFT CEO: WINDOWS OFFERS BEST VARIETY OF CONTENT TOOLS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Consumers want to access their growing libraries of videos, photos and other media on all of their electronic gadgets, and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Microsoft Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . can provide that experience, said \f28 \uc2 \f2 Steve Ballmer\f28 \uc2 \f2 , the company's chief executive. (published 0431 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: INDIA'S JINDAL SURPRISES MARKET, CUTS STAKE IN ROCKLANDS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Jindal Steel & Power Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . surprised the market Thursday by selling down part of its stake in takeover target \f28 \uc2 \f2 Rocklands Richfield Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., causing shares in the Australian company to plummet. (published 0506 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AEON 9-MONTH GROUP NET LOSS Y9.93B VS Y29.45B LOSS YR EARLIER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese retail giant Aeon Co. said Thursday it remained in the red for the nine-month period ended November, as sales continued to suffer from consumer worries over the outlook for wages and employment. (published 0620 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par MITSUBISHI RAYON: TO SELL LUCITE CHINA \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 OPERATIONS\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TO 4 FIRMS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Mitsubishi Rayon Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Thursday that unit \f28 \uc2 \f2 Lucite International Group Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . will sell a portion of its China \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to meet that country's antimonopoly requirements. (published 0649 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SEVEN & I HOLDINGS MARCH-NOVEMBER NET PROFIT FALLS 32% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Seven & i Holdings\f28 \uc2 \f2  Co. said Thursday that its revenue and net profit for the nine-month period ended November dropped at a double digit pace from a year earlier, as consumers continued to fret over the uncertain outlook for wages and employment. (published 0619 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par MINERAL RESOURCES BOOSTS POLARIS OFFER IN EFFORT TO WOO LION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Mineral Resources Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Thursday it will boost the cash component of its takeover offer for \f28 \uc2 \f2 Polaris Metals NL\f28 \uc2 \f2  if it reaches the compulsory acquisition threshold of 90% control of the target. (published 2207 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par DAIHATSU: CANCELLED 50-50 JOINT VENTURE WITH FAW JILIN AUTOMOBILE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Daihatsu Motor Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Thursday it has canceled a 50:50 joint venture in China with FAW Jilin Automobile Co. as part of its changed sales strategy in the world's biggest auto market. (published 0616 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDUSTRIAL BANK UNAUDITED 2009 NET PROFIT UP 17% AT CNY13.3B \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Industrial Bank Co., China's seventh-largest lender by market value, posted a 17% rise in unaudited 2009 net profit, reversing a 5% fall in first-half earnings amid a robust recovery in China's economy. (published 2342 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ARCELORMITTAL: NO PLAN AS OF NOW TO SCRAP INDIA STEEL PROJECTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ArcelorMittal\f28 \uc2 \f2  Chairman L.N. Mittal said Thursday he isn't satisfied with the progress on the company's ongoing projects to set up steel plants in India, but there are no plans to scrap these projects. (published 0642 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BANK MANDIRI PROPOSES TO GOVERNMENT TO SELL 7% STAKE TO PUBLIC \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 PT \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank Mandiri\f28 \uc2 \f2  has proposed to the government, which owns 67% of the bank, to sell a 7% stake in the bank to the public to increase the stock's free float. (published 0215 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: Asian Shares Mostly Lower; JAL Slides In Tokyo \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Stock markets in Asia were mostly lower Thursday as Wall Street's uninspiring performance left investors unwilling to chase stocks after their recent gains. (published 0407 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ENERGY/COMMODITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PETROCHINA UPS GAS SUPPLIES, BUT LIMITS INDUSTRIAL USE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 PetroChina Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., China's top natural gas producer, is ramping up gas supplies from its Changqing field by 30% over last year to tackle severe gas shortages in Beijing city as well as other northern regions, the parent company said Thursday. (published 0329 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA HOG PRICES MAY RISE BEFORE HOLIDAYS ON HIGH DEMAND -NDRC \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hog prices in China are likely to rise ahead of the Lunar New Year holidays due to strong demand but may ease afterwards amid ample supply, the country's economic planner said late Wednesday. (published 0259 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par MALAYSIAN PALM OIL STOCKS LIKELY NEAR 2 MLN ON SLUGGISH EXPORTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Malaysia's crude palm oil stocks may have risen to between 1.95 million and 1.98 million metric tons as of end-December due to sluggish export demand and a spike in Indonesian palm oil imports, plantation company executives and trade participants said late Wednesday. (published 0330 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TONG THAI NABON SELLS RSS3 RUBBER AT $3,020/TON, FOB -EXECUTIVE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 07-01-10 0703GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Natural rubber prices have risen above $3,000 a metric ton for the first time in 15 months and one company, Tong Thai Nabon, has sold 600 tons at $3,020/ton, free on board for January shipment, a trading executive said Thursday. (published 0445 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDIA NOT PLANNING \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ON STEEL PRICES -SECRETARY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India won't likely \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to curb steel product price hikes by domestic companies, Steel Secretary Atul Chaturvedi said Thursday. (published 0550 GMT) [ 07-01-10 0703GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 62550   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100107e617000gr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
