\par\par \b \uc2 Dow Jones Asia-Pacific Top Stories Sked For January 5\b0\par\par\uc2 1,886 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Januar 2010\par 08:04\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Following are the top Asia-Pacific stories featured on Dow Jones Newswires as of 0700 GMT. Not all stories appear on all wires. Please direct any questions orcommentstoasianewseds@dowjones.com.\par \par \uc2 MACRO/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /FIXED INCOME:\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: JAPAN FUJII VAGUE ON FUTURE, AWAITS HEALTH CHECK RESULTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's finance minister attended the first cabinet meeting of the year Tuesday despite concerns over his health, but left it unclear whether he would continue in the post if the results of a recent medical check are not good. (published 0512 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDIA PM ECONOMIC ADVISER: RBI MAY HIKE CRR TO HELP TAME INFLATION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of India\f28 \uc2 \f2  may raise the cash reserve ratio--the proportion of cash that banks are required to park at the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as reserves--to soak up liquidity in its bid to control inflation, the chairman of the prime minister's Economic Advisory Council said Tuesday. (published 0503 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: PHILIPPINES DECEMBER INFLATION SURGES, STAYS WITHIN GOAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Inflation in the Philippines accelerated at its fastest clip in eight months in December, but was still within the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's forecast range, giving authorities the leeway to keep monetary policy loose. (published 0453 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN'S DOMESTIC AUTO SALES RISE 36.5% ON YEAR IN DECEMBER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's domestic sales of new cars, trucks and buses increased 36.5% from a year earlier in December as government buying incentives boosted sales of fuel-efficient cars, the Japan Automobile Dealers Association said Tuesday. (published 0523 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SOUTH KOREA'S \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREIGN EXCHANGE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  RESERVES FALL IN DECEMBER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves fell for the first time in 10 months in December, largely due to a decline in the value of non-dollar assets as a result of the greenback's gains, the Bank of Korea said Tuesday. (published 2100 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SOUTH KOREA PLEDGED FOREIGN DIRECT INVESTMENT DOWN 1.9% IN 2009 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Foreign direct investment in South Korea fell 1.9% to $11.48 billion last year as companies trimmed overseas capital expenditure amid the global economic slowdown, the Ministry of Knowledge Economy said Tuesday. (published 0201 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SOUTH KOREA FINANCIAL WATCHDOG INTRODUCES GUIDELINES FOR \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  DERIVATIVES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's financial watchdog Tuesday unveiled guidelines to help companies better manage risks involved in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  derivatives. (published 0300 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BANK OF KOREA MAY HAVE BOUGHT AT LEAST $2 BLN TO CAP WON-TRADERS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Korea may have \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  constantly in the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market Tuesday to cap a rise in the won, several Seoul-based traders said. (published 0641 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BANK INDONESIA LIKELY BUYS DOLLAR AT IDR9,290-IDR9,305 \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  likely \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market Tuesday to cap a sharp rise in the rupiah as investors bought local assets, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dealers said. (published 0334 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PHILIPPINES '09 BUDGET DEFICIT LIKELY BELOW PHP300 BLN -OFFICIAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Philippines will likely report a budget deficit for 2009 of below PHP300 billion, Finance Undersecretary Gil Beltran said Tuesday. (published 0559 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AUSTRALIA NEW HOME SALES RISE 0.3% IN NOV VS OCT - HIA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australian new homes sales rose 0.3% in November from October, according to a survey of the country's largest builders. (published 0029 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par VIETNAM GOVERNMENT: TO KEEP TRADE DEFICIT FROM EXCEEDING $12 BILLION IN 2010 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Vietnam aims to keep its trade deficit from exceeding $12 billion, or 20% of total export revenues, in 2010 by boosting exports and controlling imports, the government said Tuesday. (published 0233 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par KOREA EXPRESS CANCELS PLAN TO ISSUE KRW120 BLN BONDS -OFFICIALS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Korea Express Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., a logistics affiliate of cash-strapped \f28 \uc2 \f2 Kumho Asiana Group\f28 \uc2 \f2 , has canceled its plan to issue KRW120 billion in corporate bonds in the wake of the parent group's financial troubles, company officials said Tuesday. (published 0509 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHANDRA ASRI MAY SELL $250 MLN BONDS THIS QUARTER - EXECUTIVE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indonesian petrochemical company PT Chandra Asri may sell up to $250 million of global bonds as early as the first quarter of this year to fund investment plans and refinance outstanding debts, an executive at Chandra Asri's parent company said Tuesday. (published 0433 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par KOREA HYDRO & NUCLEAR POWER TO HIRE BANKS FOR GLOBAL BOND SALE -SOURCES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Korea Hydro & Nuclear Power Corp., which is looking to sell global bonds, sent a request for proposals to investment banks earlier this week and will likely name lead managers for the sale next week, people familiar with the matter said Tuesday. (published 0646 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PREVIEW: BANK OF KOREA LIKELY TO KEEP KEY RATE UNCHANGED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Korea is likely to leave its base rate at an all-time low of 2.00% this month to help sustain a recovery in Asia's fourth-largest economy, economists said. (published 0504 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =PREVIEW: \f28 \uc2 \f2 BANK OF THAILAND\f28 \uc2 \f2  TO LEAVE RATES STEADY AMID LETHARGIC RECOVERY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Thailand's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is tipped to leave its benchmark interest rate on hold next week amid lethargic economic recovery and mild inflationary pressures, economists said. (published 0410 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =PREVIEW: BANK INDONESIA LIKELY TO KEEP RATE STEADY AT 6.50% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia is likely to keep its key rate unchanged at a monetary policy review this week to allow the domestic economic recovery to take hold as inflation remains mild. (published 0232 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =PREVIEW: MALAYSIA EXPORTS LIKELY UP FOR SECOND STRAIGHT MONTH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Malaysia's exports likely grew for the second straight month in November on a favorable base and gradually improving external demand, economists said. (published 0407 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 EQUITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SUMITOMO MITSUI FG TO ISSUE ABOUT Y800B IN NEW COMMON SHRS-SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Sumitomo Mitsui Financial Group Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . is likely to raise about Y800 billion by issuing common shares, a person familiar with the matter said Tuesday. (published 0536 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: JAPAN MAEHARA: COURT OPTION WON'T DETERMINE JAL REHAB FORM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's transport minister said Tuesday the way in which \f28 \uc2 \f2 Japan Airlines Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . is restructured will not be primarily determined by whether it takes place in or out of court. (published 0532 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: KUMHO UNVEILS RESTRUCTURING PLAN; CREDITORS TO MEET \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's cash-strapped \f28 \uc2 \f2 Kumho Asiana Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  Tuesday unveiled a restructuring plan that includes raising more than KRW1.3 trillion through asset sales and trimming its workforce. (published 0450 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par KDB: TO SELECT INVESTORS IN FUND TO BUY DAEWOO ENGINEERING IN 1 MONTH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Korea Development Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  aims to select investors in its private equity fund to buy a controlling stake in \f28 \uc2 \f2 Daewoo Engineering & Construction Co\f28 \uc2 \f2  in one month, the state-run bank's chairman and chief executive, Min Euoo-sung, said Tuesday. (published 0557 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TOYOTA UNVEILS CONCEPT MODEL OF NEW SMALL CAR IN INDIA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Toyota Kirloskar Motor Pvt. Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 .--the Indian unit of Japan's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Toyota Motor Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . --unveiled Tuesday the concept of its small car, Etios, at the Auto Expo in New Delhi. (published 0450 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par HONDA SMALL CAR LAUNCH IN INDIA, THAILAND BY 2011 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Honda Motor Co. Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . expects to launch a small car in India and Thailand by 2011, its executive vice president and representative director said Tuesday at the Auto Expo. (published 0535 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par VOLKSWAGEN LAUNCHES POLO HATCHBACK CAR IN INDIA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Volkswagen AG\f28 \uc2 \f2 , Europe's biggest car maker by sales, Tuesday unveiled its first hatchback in India. (published 0611 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par DATANG POWER TO BUY CHONGQING HYDROPOWER COMPANY FOR CNY1.35B \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Datang International Power Generation Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Monday it has agreed to acquire a power company in Chongqing to increase its exposure in the hydropower business. (published 0028 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par HUAWEI TECHNOLOGIES EXPECTS 2010 CONTRACT SALES $36 BLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese telecommunications equipment maker \f28 \uc2 \f2 Huawei Technologies Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Tuesday it expects contract sales this year of $36 billion, up from more than $30 billion last year. (published 0407 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SHIMAO PROPERTY 2009 CONTRACTED SALES CNY22.50 BLN; UP 88% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese developer \f28 \uc2 \f2 Shimao Property Holdings\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Monday its 2009 contracted sales totaled CNY22.50 billion, up 88% from CNY12.01 billion a year earlier. (published 0205 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par LG ELEC AIR CONDITIONING UNIT EYES KRW5 TLN SALES IN 2010 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 LG Electronics Co.'s air conditioning unit said Tuesday it expects its sales at KRW5 trillion in 2010, returning to pre-crisis levels. (published 0503 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par POWERCHIP SEMICONDUCTOR: SWUNG TO NET PROFIT IN 4TH QUARTER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Taiwan's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Powerchip Semiconductor Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Monday it swung to a net profit in the fourth quarter after 10 consecutive quarterly losses due to recovering demand and steadily rising chip prices. (published 0400 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: BUMI RESOURCES 9-MONTH NET FALLS ON COAL PRICE, TAX EXPENSE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Giant coal miner \f28 \uc2 \f2 PT Bumi Resources\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Tuesday its nine-month net profit fell 27% as lower coal prices pushed revenue down and higher tax expenses hit the bottom line. (published 0211 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: THE WAREHOUSE'S CHRISTMAS, NEW YEAR SALES DISAPPOINT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New Zealand discount general retailer \f28 \uc2 \f2 The Warehouse Group Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Tuesday that sales over the vital Christmas and New Year period were flat and so it is now expecting flat results for the six months to Jan. 31. (published 0236 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par REXCHIP ELECTRONICS: TO SET UP R&D CENTER WITH ELPIDA IN 1ST QUARTER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Rexchip Electronics Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . and its parent \f28 \uc2 \f2 Elpida Memory Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . will set up a research and development center in Taiwan to develop more advanced chip-production technology, Rexchip said Tuesday. (published 0633 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BOCOM SCHRODER FUND: ETF VALUE INTACT DESPITE DATA ENTRY ERROR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 05-01-10 0704GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank of Communications Schroder Fund Management Co. said Monday the net asset value of one of its exchange-traded funds hasn't been affected by a data entry error that led to a spike in trading volume and redemptions and a brief suspension of the fund last week. (published 0607 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par =UPDATE: MOST ASIAN SHARES UP AS RESOURCE, TECH PLAYS ADVANCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asian stock markets traded mostly higher Tuesday, bolstered by Wall Street's strong start for 2010. Resources plays gained on stronger commodity prices while technology shares were higher on optimism for chip sales this year. (published 0409 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ENERGY/COMMODITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par IRAQ DEC OIL EXPORTS UP 4% ON MONTH AT 1.977 MILLION B/D \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Iraq's crude oil exports in December were up 4% at 1.977 million barrels a day, compared with 1.902 million barrels a day in November, an Iraqi oil industry source said Monday. (published 0345 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA RIVER POLLUTION "SERIOUS" AFTER OIL SPILL - GOVT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Two tributaries of China's Yellow River have been "seriously polluted" by an oil spill, further contaminating badly tainted drinking water resources, the government said Tuesday. (published 0416 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDIA NOVEMBER IRON ORE EXPORTS UP 25% ON YEAR -TRADE BODY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's November iron ore exports rose 25% from a year earlier to 10.66 million metric tons, the country's top miners' association said Tuesday. (published 0537 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par NO WINNERS IN INDONESIA SUGAR BUY TENDER -EXECUTIVE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Four Indonesian state plantations failed to award a buy tender for 364,500 metric tons of white sugar as enough bids weren't submitted, a company executive said Tuesday. (published 0550 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDIA REPLACES MALAYSIA AS 3RD LARGEST NATURAL RUBBER PRODUCER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India replaced Malaysia as the world's third-largest producer of natural rubber in 2009 amid sharply lower output estimates for Malaysia due to adverse weather, lower yield, slow replanting, lack of fresh planting and a notable shift of acreage to oil palm in the last few years. (published 0620 GMT) [ 05-01-10 0704GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 62550   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100105e615000f4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
