\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 1,070 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Januar 2010\par 08:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: JAPAN FUJII VAGUE ON FUTURE, AWAITS HEALTH CHECK RESULTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's finance minister attended the first cabinet meeting of the year Tuesday despite concerns over his health, but left it unclear whether he would continue in the post if the results of a recent medical check are not good. (published 0512 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par INDIA PM ECONOMIC ADVISER: RBI MAY HIKE CRR TO HELP TAME INFLATION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of India\f28 \uc2 \f2  may raise the cash reserve ratio--the proportion of cash that banks are required to park at the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as reserves--to soak up liquidity in its bid to control inflation, the chairman of the prime minister's Economic Advisory Council said Tuesday. (published 0503 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: PHILIPPINES DECEMBER INFLATION SURGES, STAYS WITHIN GOAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Inflation in the Philippines accelerated at its fastest clip in eight months in December, but was still within the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's forecast range, giving authorities the leeway to keep monetary policy loose. (published 0453 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE:PBOC: MONETARY POLICY SHOULD SUPPORT RESOURCES REFORM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's monetary policy should support a long-term restructuring of the economy, including reforming the allocation of resources in the country, rather than simply targeting low inflation in the short run, People's Bank of China Gov. Zhou Xiaochuan said in a magazine article. (published 0334 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: CHINA TO EXTEND PROPERTY TAX SIMULATION - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China will extend a simulation of a new property tax system nationwide this year, signaling the introduction of the new tax is approaching, the state-run Shanghai Securities News reported Tuesday. (published 0451 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN'S DOMESTIC AUTO SALES RISE 36.5% ON YEAR IN DECEMBER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's domestic sales of new cars, trucks and buses increased 36.5% from a year earlier in December as government buying incentives boosted sales of fuel-efficient cars, the Japan Automobile Dealers Association said Tuesday. (published 0523 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par SOUTH KOREA'S \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREIGN EXCHANGE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  RESERVES FALL IN DECEMBER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves fell for the first time in 10 months in December, largely due to a decline in the value of non-dollar assets as a result of the greenback's gains, the Bank of Korea said Tuesday. (published 2100 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par SOUTH KOREA PLEDGED FOREIGN DIRECT INVESTMENT DOWN 1.9% IN 2009 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Foreign direct investment in South Korea fell 1.9% to $11.48 billion last year as companies trimmed overseas capital expenditure amid the global economic slowdown, the Ministry of Knowledge Economy said Tuesday. (published 0201 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par SOUTH KOREA FINANCIAL WATCHDOG INTRODUCES GUIDELINES FOR \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  DERIVATIVES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's financial watchdog Tuesday unveiled guidelines to help companies better manage risks involved in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  derivatives. (published 0300 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BANK OF KOREA MAY HAVE BOUGHT AT LEAST $2 BLN TO CAP WON-TRADERS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Korea may have \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  constantly in the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market Tuesday to cap a rise in the won, several Seoul-based traders said. (published 0641 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BANK INDONESIA LIKELY BUYS DOLLAR AT IDR9,290-IDR9,305 \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  likely \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market Tuesday to cap a sharp rise in the rupiah as investors bought local assets, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dealers said. (published 0334 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par PHILIPPINES '09 BUDGET DEFICIT LIKELY BELOW PHP300 BLN -OFFICIAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Philippines will likely report a budget deficit for 2009 of below PHP300 billion, Finance Undersecretary Gil Beltran said Tuesday. (published 0559 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIA NEW HOME SALES RISE 0.3% IN NOV VS OCT - HIA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australian new homes sales rose 0.3% in November from October, according to a survey of the country's largest builders. (published 0029 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par VIETNAM GOVERNMENT: TO KEEP TRADE DEFICIT FROM EXCEEDING $12 BILLION IN 2010 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Vietnam aims to keep its trade deficit from exceeding $12 billion, or 20% of total export revenues, in 2010 by boosting exports and controlling imports, the government said Tuesday. (published 0233 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =DATA SNAP: KAZAKHSTAN DECEMBER CPI UP 0.6%; 2009 INFLATION AT 6.2% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Kazakhstan's consumer price index rose 0.6% on the month in December after increasing 0.5% the previous month, bringing the full-year inflation to 6.2%, the country's statistics agency said Tuesday. (published 0558 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par KOREA EXPRESS CANCELS PLAN TO ISSUE KRW120 BLN BONDS -OFFICIALS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Korea Express Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., a logistics affiliate of cash-strapped \f28 \uc2 \f2 Kumho Asiana Group\f28 \uc2 \f2 , has canceled its plan to issue KRW120 billion in corporate bonds in the wake of the parent group's financial troubles, company officials said Tuesday. (published 0509 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHANDRA ASRI MAY SELL $250 MLN BONDS THIS QUARTER - EXECUTIVE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indonesian petrochemical company PT Chandra Asri may sell up to $250 million of global bonds as early as the first quarter of this year to fund investment plans and refinance outstanding debts, an executive at Chandra Asri's parent company said Tuesday. (published 0433 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par KOREA HYDRO & NUCLEAR POWER TO HIRE BANKS FOR GLOBAL BOND SALE -SOURCES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Korea Hydro & Nuclear Power Corp., which is looking to sell global bonds, sent a request for proposals to investment banks earlier this week and will likely name lead managers for the sale next week, people familiar with the matter said Tuesday. (published 0646 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par    ======== DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======== \par  \par  \par =PREVIEW: BANK OF KOREA LIKELY TO KEEP KEY RATE UNCHANGED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Korea is likely to leave its base rate at an all-time low of 2.00% this month to help sustain a recovery in Asia's fourth-largest economy, economists said. (published 0504 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =PREVIEW: \f28 \uc2 \f2 BANK OF THAILAND\f28 \uc2 \f2  TO LEAVE RATES STEADY AMID LETHARGIC RECOVERY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Thailand's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is tipped to leave its benchmark interest rate on hold next week amid lethargic economic recovery and mild inflationary pressures, economists said. (published 0410 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =PREVIEW: BANK INDONESIA LIKELY TO KEEP RATE STEADY AT 6.50% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia is likely to keep its key rate unchanged at a monetary policy review this week to allow the domestic economic recovery to take hold as inflation remains mild. (published 0232 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =PREVIEW: MALAYSIA EXPORTS LIKELY UP FOR SECOND STRAIGHT MONTH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Malaysia's exports likely grew for the second straight month in November on a favorable base and gradually improving external demand, economists said. (published 0407 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  OPTIONS: DLR/YEN OPTIONS FALL; HEDGE FUNDS TAKE PROFITS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Dollar/yen \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  options declined in Asia on Tuesday as hedge funds sold upside protection amid dollar weakness. (published 0337 GMT) [ 05-01-10 0700GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100105e615000en\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
