\par\par \b \uc2 Indonesia Market factors to watch - Dec 22\b0\par\par\uc2 807 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Dezember 2009\par 03:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, Dec 22 (Reuters) - Following is a list of events in Indonesia as well as news stories and press reports which may influence financial markets.\par \par \uc2  (Reuters welcomes your feedback, and for any queries please contact Sara Webb in Jakarta editorial on +6221 384 6364 or via email at sara.webb@thomsonreuters.com or on Reuters messaging sara.webb.reuters.com@reuters.net)\par \par \uc2  WHAT IS HAPPENING IN INDONESIA, ALL TIMES LOCAL FOLLOWED BY GMT\par \par \uc2  (The inclusion of diary items does not necessarily mean that Reuters will cover the event)\par \par \uc2  - Parliamentary inquiry committee to call Vice President Boediono for questioning about the \uc2 Bank Century\uc2  bailout.\par \par \uc2  - Economics faculty of University of Indonesia to host a discussion on 2009 Political Economy Review, 1300-1500 (0600-0800)\par \par \uc2  PRESS DIGEST\par \par \uc2  - TERROR CELLS STILL ACTIVELY RECRUITING MEMBERS - POLICE\par \par \uc2  Brig. Gen. Tito Karnavian, head of police anti-terror unit Detachment 88, said that cells in Indonesia are still actively recruiting new members and planning attacks, and that police had managed to trace the funding for terror activities. (Jakarta Post)\par \par \uc2  - BERLIAN LAJU TO SPEND $140 MLN ON SHIPS\par \par \uc2  Indonesian shipping firm \uc2 Berlian Laju Tanker\uc2   will spend $140 million to buy four new ships from Japan next year, said investor relations manager Peter Chayson.\par \par \uc2  MARKET SNAPSHOTS\par \par \uc2  * Indonesia <.JKSE> slid to its lowest since Dec. 1, with Telkom Indonesia  dropping 6 percent and \uc2 Astra International\uc2   down more than 3 percent. That selling in part reflected weakness elsewhere in the region on Friday when Jakarta was closed for a market holiday. [.SO]\par \par \uc2  * U.S. stocks rose on Monday, with the Nasdaq hitting a 15-month high after a healthcare reform bill advanced in the Senate and brokerages upgraded two Dow components on improving profit prospects.[.N]\par \par \uc2  * Oil prices fell on Monday as a stronger dollar offset cold weather in the United States and Europe and reports of pipeline snags in oil exporters Iraq and Nigeria. [O/R]\par \par \uc2  * For global market news, click on [MKTS/GLOB]\par \par \uc2  * Malaysian crude palm oil futures dropped 2.5 percent on Monday, retreating from last week's six-and-a-half month highs on Friday's drop in U.S. soyoil prices as well as slowing exports. [POI/]\par \par \uc2  * In Indonesia, the state marketing centre, based in Jakarta, sold 7,500 tonnes of palm oil at a top price of 7,289 rupiah ($0.768) per kg against 7,410 rupiah last Thursday. The market was closed on Friday for a public holiday. [OILS/TEND]\par \par \uc2  * To see the top news on Indonesia's economy click on [ID:nIDECONOMY]. For a take a look on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  click on [ID:nIDCENBANK] and for the bond market click on [ID:nIDBOND]. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ---------------------MARKET SNAPSHOT @ 2308 GMT -------------\par                 INSTRUMENT    LAST       PCT CHG   NET CHG\par S&P 500             <.SPX>      1,114.05      1.05     11.580\par USD/JPY             <JPY=>         91.18      0.07      0.060\par 10-YR US TSY YLD    <US10YT=RR>  3.6803         --      0.000\par SPOT GOLD           <XAU=>     $1,091.15     -0.16     -1.700\par US CRUDE            <CLc1>        $72.47     -1.21     -0.890\par DOW JONES           <.DJI>      10414.14      0.83      85.25\par ASIA ADRS           <.BKAS>       125.07     -0.41       0.51\par -------------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  FOR KEY GLOBAL ECONOMIC NEWS, SEE [TOP/MACRO]\par  FOR TOP NEWS ON ASIAN COMPANIES [TOP/EQA]\par  FOR ECONOMIC \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  RELATED NEWS, HIT [FXNEWS]\par  FOR WHAT INVESTORS ARE SAYING ABOUT DEALS [DEALTALK/]\par  STOCKS - BUY OR SELL? [BUYSELL/] IN THE NEWS, REUTERS\par INDONESIA (Click on [ID-RTRS]) Papuans threaten to block\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Freeport's mine       [ID:nN21251480] Indonesia firm to mine\par for copper in Zambia     [ID:nLDE5BK1I5] World Bank to lend\par $500mln for geothermal project[ID:nJAK19649] Anti-trust agency\par seeks bigger role in M&A       [ID:nJAK43253] Indonesia palm\par oil export tax at 3 pct in Jan   [ID:nJAK245267] Indonesia to\par extend low import duty for sugar    [ID:nJAK53206] Bakrie\par Sumatera sees higher output               [ID:nJAK16842]\par Indonesia may miss oil output target in '09,'10  [ID:nJAK48673]\par Indonesia eyes $316 mln retail sukuk issue in Feb[ID:nJAK45146]\par Details of Indonesia's retail sukuk              [ID:nJAK46322]\par Bulog rice stocks seen up, paves way for exports [ID:nJAK17002]\par Investors should buy into stock sell-off - CLSA  \par [ID:nJAK6193]\par   ASIA MARKETS NEWS - For an outlook of Asian stock trading,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 click on [STXNEWS/AS] - The dollar's broad strength weighed\par down most Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Monday, with the high-yielding\par Indonesian rupiah hitting a one-month low and prompting the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . [EMRG/FRX] - \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's stock index\par fell more than 3 percent to its lowest in almost three weeks on\par Monday, leading declines in other major regional markets, with\par big caps such as Telkom Indonesia and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Astra International\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par leading the way. [.SO]\par  (Reporting by Telly Nathalia and Tyagita Silka)\par \pa