\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE: Bank  \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia \highlight\uc2  Has "No Choice" But To Continue With  \highlight22\uc2 FX Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 489 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Dezember 2009\par 09:19\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 (Adds comment from Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's acting governor and background.)\par \par \uc2 By Reuben Carder and Costas Paris\par \par \uc2 OF DOW JONES NEWSWIRES\par \par \uc2 JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  has "no choice" but to continue \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to stabilize the dollar-rupiah rate, and is likely to raise its policy rate in the first or second quarter next year as price pressures increase, a person familiar with the situation said Friday.\par \par \uc2 The person told Dow Jones Newswires that the benchmark rate is likely to be raised from the current 6.50% in the first or second quarter of next year. The timing and size of the hikes will depend on inflation, he said, which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  anticipates will be driven by rising domestic demand, as well as higher prices for commodities and crude oil.\par \par \uc2 Separately, Bank Indonesia's acting governor Darmin Nasution said later Friday that inflationary pressures in Indonesia are expected to increase in the second quarter of next year.\par \par \uc2 Nasution reiterated an earlier forecast that annual inflation this year is likely to be around 2.9%, softer than last year's 11.1%. Indonesia uses the on-year price increase in December as its annual inflation rate.\par \par \uc2 Besides the high-base effect last year, easing energy and commodity prices around the world as well as the rupiah's appreciation of around 15% so far this year have brought inflation to its lowest levels in many years.\par \par \uc2 Bank Indonesia officials didn't specify the size of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Market participants estimate Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  has bought or sold dollars on many occasions this year--often as much as $100 million or more in a single day--to cap sharp dollar-rupiah movements amid volatility in regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Bank Indonesia doesn't generally target a specific exchange rate.\par \par \uc2 Indonesia's Chamber of Commerce and Industry has pressured Bank Indonesia to cut rates further from the current record-low level to give extra impetus to the economy, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't consider there's enough room for more cuts, the person said. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has cut a total of 300 basis points since it started easing in December 2008.\par \par \uc2 The Chamber of Commerce didn't immediately respond to a request for comment.\par \par \uc2 The person added that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is of the view that the high inflation base effect from 2008 has yet to dissipate.\par \par \uc2 The government in mid-2008 raised retail fuel prices by an average of 30%, sending inflation to multiyear highs. The high base effect, and a downturn in the domestic economy, are likely to reduce Indonesia's inflation rate to a record low of 3.5% or less this year, officials have previously said.\par \par \uc2 -By Costas Paris and Reuben Carder, Dow Jones Newswires; 62 21 3983 1277; Reuben.Carder@dowjones.com [ 11-12-09 0819GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020091211e5cb000k7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
