\par\par \b \uc2 Indonesian c.bank  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2  to defend rupiah-traders\b0\par\par\uc2 144 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Dezember 2009\par 04:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Dec 9 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday to support the rupiah, trying to set a floor near the 9,500 per dollar level, traders said.\par \par \uc2  "BI (the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) has been selling dollars from the market opening," said a dealer in Jakarta.\par \par \uc2  The high-yielding rupiah <IDR=> fell 0.6 percent to 9,495 to the dollar due to concerns about debt woes for Greece and Dubai, but it later stablised as local exporters also sold dollars, traders said.\par \par \uc2  The rupiah is up 16 percent against the dollar this year, making it the best-performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Asia. Indonesian officials have predicted it will strengthen further next year.  (Reporting by Kevin Yao; Editing by Neil Fullick)    \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDONESIA-RUPIAH (URGENT)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|IF|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020091209e5c90004j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
