\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE: Bank  \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia \highlight\uc2 : Local Dollar Demand Outstrips Supply\b0\par\par\uc2 484 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Dezember 2009\par 06:30\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 (Adds suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , background)\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     By I Made Sentana \par     Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--Demand for the U.S. dollar in Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market is greater than the available supply at the moment, a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official said Monday, suggesting that Bank Indonesia won't try to slow capital inflows that have boosted values of local assets this year.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will, however, guard against volatility in the dollar-rupiah exchange rate ahead of expected capital inflows into emerging-market assets next year, Deputy Governor Budi Mulya said on the sidelines of a seminar when asked whether Bank Indonesia would consider curbing short-term capital inflows.\par \par \uc2 "The characteristics of our market are different" from those of other countries (that have moved to curb inflows)," he said on the sidelines of a seminar.\par \par \uc2 "In the local market, there is still excess demand" for dollars, he said.\par \par \uc2 His remark indicates that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  views inflows of capital as necessary to meet market demand for the dollar. U.S. dollar liquidity in the country is quite low due to massive fund outflows that occurred late last year.\par \par \uc2 The domestic economy's relatively strong performance and improving political stability have, however, attracted capital inflows of late. The rupiah has gained more than 15% against the dollar since January, while the benchmark stock index is up around 80%.\par \par \uc2 The market was abuzz with speculation last month that Bank Indonesia would move to limit inflows of short-term funds after Deputy Governor Hartadi Sarwono said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would study the pros and cons of limiting foreign ownership in its short-term notes. Sarwono later said that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  wouldn't implement such a policy.\par \par \uc2 Mulya reiterated Monday that Bank Indonesia will maintain its current policy on exchange-rate movements. From time to time, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sells the U.S. dollar against the rupiah, and vice versa, to cap sharp moves in the exchange rate.\par \par \uc2 Earlier Monday, Bank Indonesia was thought to have sold $25 million to $50 million between IDR9,460 and IDR9,465 to head off weakness in the rupiah as upbeat U.S. November employment data gave the dollar a boost against regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 A 0.6% fall in local stocks and dollar-buying by local companies to pay year-end debts added to the local unit's weakness, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said.\par \par \uc2 The dollar retreated to IDR9,455 following the suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from an intraday peak of IDR9,465. The dollar fetched IDR9,415 late Friday.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said that the market wasn't affected by Mulya's subsequent remarks on demand for the U.S. dollar as those were in line with market expectations.\par \par \uc2 -By I Made Sentana, Dow Jones Newswires; 62 21 3983 1277; I-Made.Sentana@dowjones.com (Reuben Carder contributed to this article) [ 07-12-09 0530GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020091207e5c70009r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
