\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE: Bank Indonesia Defends Rupiah; Likely Sold $50m-$100M\b0\par\par\uc2 321 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 November 2009\par 10:31\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 (Updates rupiah level, adds background)\par \par \uc2 By Reuben Carder\par \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES\par \par \uc2 JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  was suspected to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to slow the rupiah's fall Thursday when several other regional central banks were reportedly trying to rein in their surging \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Bank Indonesia likely sold between $50 million and $100 million between IDR9,450 and IDR9,460 to prevent the rupiah from falling too sharply during the afternoon session, the dealers said. They attributed the rupiah's weakness to a comeback by the dollar against the majors and a fall in the domestic stock market, which lost 2.8%.\par \par \uc2 Monetary authorities in the Philippines, Thailand, Singapore and South Korea appeared to sell their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  Thursday, fending off a slide in the dollar that threatens their export-oriented economies. Their \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  were, however, small, traders said.\par \par \uc2 The domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was "just leveling out the movements" in the market rather than protecting a specific level, a dealer said. Dealers said liquidity was thin ahead of an Islamic holiday Friday, exaggerating the market's movements.\par \par \uc2 Bank Indonesia doesn't target a level for the rupiah, but prefers a stronger local unit to help fight imported inflation and to support capital-goods imports. It \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market from time to time to cap excess volatility.\par \par \uc2 The dollar opened the day's domestic trading session at IDR9,365, compared with IDR9,400 in late Asian trade Wednesday. It rose to a high of IDR9,460 during the afternoon session before easing to IDR9,445 subsequently.\par \par \uc2 One \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer said that Bank Indonesia will probably be comfortable letting the dollar fall to around IDR9,200 for now and isn't likely to prop up the dollar as long as it stays above that level.\par \par \uc2 -By Reuben Carder, Dow Jones Newswires; 62 21 3983 1277; Reuben.Carder@dowjones.com [ 26-11-09 0931GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020091126e5bq000s2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw442\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6630\pichgoal600
