Directive"). The Savings Directive requires Member States (as \par defined below) to provide to the tax authorities of other Member States details \par of payments of interest and other similar income paid by a person to an \par individual in another Member State, except that Austria, Belgium and Luxembourg \par will instead impose a withholding system for a transitional period unless during \par such period they elect otherwise. \par  \par  \par The Bank undertakes that it will ensure that it maintains a paying agent in a \par country which is a member of the European Union (a "Member State") that will not \par be obliged to withhold or deduct tax pursuant to the Savings Directive. \par  \par  \par 2.United States Tax Matters \par     A) United States Internal Revenue Service Circular 230 Notice: To ensure \par compliance with Internal Revenue Service Circular 230, prospective investors are \par hereby notified that: (a) any discussion of U.S. federal tax issues contained or \par referred to in this Pricing Supplement, the Prospectus or any other document \par referred to herein is not intended or written to be used, and cannot be used, by \par prospective investors for the purpose of avoiding penalties that may be imposed \par on them under the United States Internal Revenue Code; (b) such discussions are \par written for use in connection with the promotion or marketing of the \par transactions or matters addressed herein; and (c) prospective investors should \par seek advice based on their particular circumstances from an independent tax \par advisor. \par     B) The "Tax Matters" section of the Prospectus and any tax disclosure in \par this pricing supplement is of a general nature only, is not exhaustive of all \par possible tax considerations and is not intended to be, and should not be \par construed to be, legal, business or tax advice to any particular prospective \par investor. Each prospective investor should consult its own tax advisor as to the \par particular tax consequences to it of the acquisition, ownership, and disposition \par of the Notes, including the effects of applicable U.S. federal, state, and local \par tax laws and non-U.S. tax laws and possible changes in tax laws. \par  \par  \par     C) Due to a change in law since the date of the Prospectus, the second \par paragraph of "-Payments of Interest" under the United States Holders section \par should be read as follows: "Interest paid by the Bank on the Notes constitutes \par income from sources outside the United States but will, depending on your \par circumstances, be "passive" or "general" income for purposes of computing the \par foreign tax credit." \par  \par  \par     D) Due to a change in law since the date of the Prospectus, the fourth \par paragraph of "-Purchase, Sale and Retirement of the Notes" under the United \par States Holders section should be read as follows: "Capital gain of a \par noncorporate United States holder that is recognized in taxable years beginning \par before January 1, 2011 is generally taxed at a maximum rate of 15% where the \par holder has a holding period greater than one year." \par 3.Noteholders should consult their own tax advisors concerning the consequences \par of owning the Notes in their particular circumstances under the Internal Revenue \par Code and the laws of any other taxing jurisdiction. \par  \par  \par 4.    Additional Investment Considerations: \par  \par  \par The Notes offered by this Pricing Supplement are complex financial instruments \par and may not be suitable for certain investors. Investors intending to purchase \par the Notes should consult with their tax and financial advisors to ensure that \par the intended purchase meets the investment objective before making such \par purchase. \par  \par  \par There are various risks associated with the Notes including, but not limited to, \par exchange rate risk, price risk and liquidity risk. Investors should consult with \par their own financial, legal and accounting advisors about the risks associated \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 20-11-09 0700GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with an investment in these Notes, the appropriate tools to analyze that \par investment, and the suitability of the investment in each investor's particular \par circumstances. Holders of the Notes should also consult with their professional \par tax advisors regarding tax laws applicable to them. \par  \par  \par The Bank will hedge its obligations under the Notes by entering into a swap \par transaction with an affiliate of the Dealer as swap counterparty. Assuming no \par change in market conditions or any other relevant factors, the price, if any, at \par which the Dealer or another purchaser might be willing to purchase Notes in a \par secondary market transaction is expected to be lower, and could be substantially \par lower, than the original issue price of the Notes. This is due to a number of \par factors, including that (i) the potential profit to the secondary market \par purchaser of the Notes may be incorporated into any offered price and (ii) the \par cost of funding used to value the Notes in the secondary market is expected to \par be higher than our actual cost of funding incurred in connection with the \par issuance of the Notes. In addition, the original issue price of the Notes \par included, and secondary market prices are likely to exclude, the projected \par profit that our swap counterparty or its affiliates may realize in connection \par with this swap. Further, as a result of dealer discounts, mark-ups or other \par transaction costs, any of which may be significant, the original issue price may \par differ from values determined by pricing models used by our swap counterparty or \par other potential purchasers of the Notes in secondary market transactions. \par  \par  \par Payment of each Interest Amount and the Redemption Amount will be based on the \par IDR Rate, which is a measure of the rate of exchange between the Indonesian \par Rupiah and the USD. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  exchange rates are volatile and will affect the \par holder's return. In addition, the government of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  can from time to time \par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market. These \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  or other \par governmental actions could adversely affect the value of the Notes, as well as \par the yield (in USD terms) on the Notes and the amount payable at maturity or upon \par acceleration. Even in the absence of governmental action directly affecting \par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  exchange rates, political or economic developments in Indonesia or \par elsewhere could lead to significant and sudden changes in the exchange rate \par between the Indonesian Rupiah and the USD. \par  \par  \par The Indonesian Rupiah is an emerging market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . Emerging market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par may be subject to particularly substantial volatility, as well as to government \par actions including \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  controls, devaluations and other matters which could \par materially and adversely affect the value of the Notes. \par  \par  \par The methodologies for determining the IDR Rate may result in a Redemption Amount \par (or Early Redemption Amount, as the case may be) of the Notes, or an Interest \par Amount on the Notes, being significantly less than anticipated or less than what \par an alternative methodology for determining the IDR-USD exchange rate would \par yield. \par  \par  \par INTER-AMERICAN DEVELOPMENT BANK \par By: \par Name:Edward Bartholomew \par Title:Chief Financial Officer and \par  \par General Manager, Finance Department \par  \par This information is provided by RNS \par             The company news service from the London Stock Exchange \par    END \par  \par  IODUWRARKARAAUA \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 20-11-09 0700GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument RNS0000020091120e5bk00006\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
