\par\par \b \uc2 Dow Jones Asia-Pacific Top Stories Sked For October 28\b0\par\par\uc2 2,495 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Oktober 2009\par 08:08\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Following are the top Asia-Pacific stories featured on Dow Jones Newswires as of 0700 GMT. Not all stories appear on all wires. Please direct any questions or comments to asianewseds@dowjones.com.\par \par \uc2 MACRO/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /FIXED INCOME:\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par =UPDATE: JAPAN RETAIL SALES FALL AS BIG RETAILERS STRUGGLE TO DRAW CUSTOMERS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's overall retail sales declined for the 13th straight month in September with a 1.4% on-year drop, the government said Wednesday, as even super-low-priced own-brand goods struggle to combat low consumer confidence. (published 0413 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: AUSTRALIA 3Q INFLATION ENOUGH TO FUEL RATE HIKE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's consumer price inflation picked up pace in the third quarter, bolstering expectations that the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of Australia\f28 \uc2 \f2  will further raise interest rates at its policy meeting next Tuesday. (published 0408 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par RBA ASST GOV: BANKS ROBUST, WORST NOW WELL OVER FOR ECONOMY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's economy is now well beyond the worst of the global financial crisis and its banking system remains robust and profitable, carrying a minimum of bad loans on its books. (published 0000 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: KOREA CURRENT ACCOUNT SURPLUS DOUBLES IN SEPTEMBER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's current-account surplus more than doubled in September from August, driven by stronger exports and inflows of foreign capital from investors attracted by the country's rapid economic recovery. (published 0340 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE:VIETNAM \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  KEEPING RATE STEADY TILL YEAR-END \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Vietnam's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said Wednesday that it will keep its benchmark rate unchanged for the rest of the year as part of efforts to stabilize the economy, with analysts saying a hike is unlikely until mid-2010. (published 0507 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BANK INDONESIA LIKELY SOLD AROUND $50M BETWEEN IDR9,600 AND IDR9,610 -DEALERS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  likely \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market Wednesday, selling about $50 million in the morning trading session to slow a sharp fall in the rupiah against the U.S. dollar, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dealers said. (published 0414 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE:NOBLE GROUP RAISES US$2.4 BILLION VIA LOAN SYNDICATION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Singapore-listed Noble Group Wednesday said that it has raised US$2.4 billion through loan syndication, making it the largest U.S. dollar syndicated corporate loan in Asia Pacific so far this year. (published 0524 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =DATA SNAP: INDIA SEP INFRASTRUCTURE OUTPUT UP 4.0% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's infrastructure output growth slowed to 4.0% on year in September from 7.8% in August, the government said in a statement Wednesday. (published 0521 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par RBI GOPINATH: COMPULSION TO EXIT EASY POLICY MORE IN INDIA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India may have to exit its easy monetary policy stance before other economies, a deputy governor of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of India\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Wednesday. (published 0455 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par HK GOVERNMENT MAY \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  IN PROPERTY MARKET IF NEEDED - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hong Kong Financial Secretary John Tsang told local property developers Tuesday the government may \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the property market if necessary to protect people's livelihoods and consumers' interests, a person who attended a high-profile meeting between the government and developers said Wednesday. (published 0630 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AUSTRALIAN SKILLED VACANCIES INDEX +1.9% IN OCT VS SEP \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 An index of job vacancies for skilled workers in Australia rose by 1.9% in October from September but still is down 44% from October last year, the Department of Employment and Workplace Relations said Wednesday. (published 0016 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE:NEW ZEALAND OCTOBER BUSINESS CONFIDENCE HOLDING STRONG \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New Zealand's business confidence remained strong in October, according to a survey released Wednesday, reinforcing recent evidence the domestic economy has turned a corner after a protracted recession. (published 0248 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDIKA ENERGY SEEKS TO PAY AROUND 9.75% YIELD FOR USD BOND - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indonesia's \f28 \uc2 \f2 PT Indika Energy Tbk\f28 \uc2 \f2 , through its unit Indo Integrated Energy, is looking to pay a yield of around 9.75% for its US$230-million global bond on offer, a person familiar with the deal said Wednesday. (published 0315 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: AGILE PROPERTY TO SELL $400M 7-YEAR USD BOND - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese developer \f28 \uc2 \f2 Agile Property Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . plans to sell US$400 million worth of seven-year U.S. dollar-denominated bonds, a person familiar with the deal said Wednesday. (published 0546 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AUCKLAND AIRPORT ANNOUNCES NZ$125 MILLION RETAIL BOND OFFER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Auckland International Airport Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Wednesday it would offer up to NZ$125 million worth of retail bonds. (published 0355 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par MALAYSIA UNVEILS NEW MEASURES FOR AUTO INDUSTRY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Malaysia has announced a raft of measures including lifting a freeze on auto manufacturing licenses and giving new incentives for hybrid electric car making, in bid to make the country an automotive production hub in the region, a government official said Wednesday. (published 0250 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA 1ST-HALF OUTWARD DIRECT INVESTMENT IN AFRICA $875M; UP 78.6% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's outward direct investment in Africa's non-financial sectors rose 78.6% to $875 million in the first half, the highest growth rate for Chinese investment in any geographical region, government data showed. (published 0538 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par THAI \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : COMMERCIAL BANK NPLS 5.7% AT END-SEPTEMBER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Thai commercial banks' gross non-performing loans at the end of September dropped marginally to 5.7% of total loans, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Thailand\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Wednesday. (published 0653 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDONESIA MINISTER: AIM TO REDUCE UNEMPLOYMENT BY HALF IN 5 YEARS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indonesia aims to reduce by half its unemployment levels over the next five years through better economic growth, Minister for Manpower and Transmigration Muhaimin Iskandar said. (published 0229 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =PREVIEW: KOREA TRADE SURPLUS LIKELY $2 BILLION IN OCTOBER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's trade surplus likely shrank in October from a month earlier as exports were relatively sluggish due to fewer working days in the month, while imports rose following gains in global oil and raw-material prices, economists said. (published 0659 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =PREVIEW: KOREA INDUSTRIAL OUTPUT LIKELY UP 6.8% IN SEPTEMBER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's industrial output probably rose at its fastest pace in more than a year in September due to increased demand ahead of Chusok holidays, with carmakers and chip makers likely to have led the way, economists said. (published 0241 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =MONEY TALKS: YIELD WON'T BE A MAJOR FRIEND FOR THE US DOLLAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The U.S. dollar is coming up for air. But probably not for long. The hardcore selling of the greenback in recent weeks has tapered off, with the euro in particular giving back a little ground and higher risk \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  like the Australian dollar looking a bit toppish. But don't presume this will be a major respite. (published 0003 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 EQUITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par =3RD UPDATE: TELSTRA DOESN'T WANT NBN STAKE IF NO GUARANTEES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Telstra Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . executives said Wednesday that the company does not want a stake in the Australian government's planned national broadband network if there are no guarantees of returns for its shareholders. (published 0337 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: SINGTEL MAY FLOAT AUSTRALIAN UNIT OPTUS - SOURCES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Singapore Telecommunications Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . is considering selling a minority stake in its Australian unit Optus through an initial public offering in Australia that could raise between US$4 billion and US$5 billion, two people familiar with the situation said Wednesday. (published 0422 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =4TH UPDATE: \f28 \uc2 \f2 NATIONAL AUSTRALIA BANK\f28 \uc2 \f2  FY NET A$2.6B, DOWN 43% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 National Australia Bank Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Wednesday full year net profit fell 43% on year, as rising bad debts and one-time tax and legal charges offset higher revenues. (published 0518 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: MONEX, ORIX AGREE TO CAPITAL TIE-UP, BROKERAGE MERGER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Monex Group Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Orix Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Wednesday they have agreed to a capital tie-up and a merger of brokerage \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by May 2010. (published 0439 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: CHINA STEEL 3RD-QUARTER PRETAX PFT FALLS 28% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China Steel Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Wednesday its third-quarter unaudited pretax profit fell 28% from a year earlier but rose sharply from the second quarter because of a rebound in steel product prices and inventory writebacks. (published 0419 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: COSCO END-SEPTEMBER REALIZED LOSS ON DERIVATIVES CNY4.17B-SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China Ocean Shipping Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., or Cosco, incurred a realized loss of CNY4.17 billion from derivatives trading as of the end of September, a person familiar with the situation told Dow Jones Newswires on Wednesday. (published 0420 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TRINITY RAISES HK$746 MLN IN HK IPO; PRICED NEAR TOP END - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Retailer Trinity Ltd. raised HK$746 million from an initial public offering ahead of a Hong Kong listing, after pricing the deal near the top end of the indicative range, a person familiar with the situation said Wednesday. (published 0647 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE:EXCELLENCE SHELVES $1B HK IPO;YUZHOU PRICED AT LOW END \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese developer \f28 \uc2 \f2 Excellence Real Estate Group Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . has shelved its up to US$1 billion Hong Kong initial public offering because of market conditions, amid weakening investor interest in the city's equities market. (published 0350 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: SAMSUNG SEES GLOBAL MEMORY CHIPS IN SHORT SUPPLY 2010 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Samsung Electronics Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Wednesday that the global semiconductor market is expected to see a "slight" shortage in the supply of memory chips next year. (published 0523 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: ACER CEO: FIRM'S 4TH-QUARTER REVENUE TO RISE 25% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Acer Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . expects its revenue to increase 25% in the fourth quarter from a year earlier, company \f28 \uc2 \f2 Chief Executive Gianfranco Lanci\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Wednesday. (published 0551 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: THAI UNION FROZEN TIPS RECORD 2009 NET PFT OF THB3B \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 28-10-09 0708GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Thai Union Frozen Products PCL\f28 \uc2 \f2  expects to post a record annual profit of THB3 billion this year as margins rise after a fall in raw material prices, President Thiraphong Chansiri said Wednesday. (published 0335 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SPICEJET\f28 \uc2 \f2  SECOND QUARTER NET LOSS INR1.01 BLN VS INR1.98 BLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indian low cost airline \f28 \uc2 \f2 SpiceJet Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Wednesday said its net loss for the second quarter narrowed to INR1.01 billion from INR1.98 billion a year earlier. (published 0320 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: KINGFISHER AIR 2Q LOSS NARROWS ON LOWER FUEL,STAFF COSTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Kingfisher Airlines Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Wednesday its second quarter net loss narrowed from a year earlier because of lower fuel and staff costs. (published 0525 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE:HCL TECH 1Q NET PROFIT DOWN 10% MAINLY ON HEDGE LOSSES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's \f28 \uc2 \f2 HCL Technologies Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Wednesday posted a better than expected fiscal first quarter consolidated net profit, even as it fell about 10% from a year earlier, hurt mainly by hedging losses and the continued impact of the economic slowdown. (published 0455 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: OCBC 3RD QUARTER NET PROFIT UP 12%, BEATS MARKET FORECASTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Singapore's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Oversea-Chinese Banking Corp. Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2  on Wednesday reported a much higher-than-consensus 12% rise in third-quarter net profit from a year earlier, bolstered by gains in interest, insurance, trading and investments income and lower loss provisions. (published 0606 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: DIGI.COM 3Q NET DOWN 9.6%;PROMISES 80% DIVIDEND PAYOUT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Mobile phone operator \f28 \uc2 \f2 Digi.Com Bhd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Wednesday its third-quarter net profit slipped 9.6% from a year earlier, but is planning to pay higher dividends in 2010 on expectations of better quarters ahead. (published 0622 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: ASIAN SHARES LOWER AS SHIPPERS FALTER, BUT HONDA UP \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asian share markets were lower Wednesday as shipping stocks and shipbuilders fell on worries about the strength of the global economic recovery, though Honda was buoyant in Tokyo after lifting its earnings forecast. (published 0413 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ENERGY/COMMODITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par =CHINA ENERGY WATCH: PIPELINE TO IGNITE RUSSIAN OIL PDT SALES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Russia isn't just targeting higher crude oil sales to China when it brings online a multibillion dollar pipeline next year. It hopes to ramp up exports of oil products as well. (published 0442 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PHILIPPINES SETS 563,000-TONS ANNUAL RICE ALLOCATION FOR LOCAL COMPANIES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Philippines will allow private-sector traders to import up to 563,000 metric tons of rice a year prior to a planned removal of quantitative restrictions on the grain in 2012, the state-owned National Food Authority said Wednesday. (published 0442 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =INTERVIEW: PHILIPPINES TO BUY MORE LOCAL RICE NEXT YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Philippine National Food Authority plans to buy more rice from the domestic market next year than this year's target volume of 1 million tons in a bid to encourage farmers to plant more of the crop. (published 0408 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PHILIPPINES EXPECTS REPLAY OF 2008 RICE CRISIS -AG SECY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Philippine Agriculture Secretary Arthur Yap said Wednesday that the country expects an imminent replay of the 2008 global rice crisis, when prices soared to record levels--in excess of $1,000 per metric ton. (published 0259 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA AIMS TO CONSOLIDATE MINERAL RESOURCE EXPLORATION SECTOR BY END-2010 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China aims to complete a consolidation of its mineral resource exploration sector by the end of 2010, the Ministry of Land and Resources said, citing a statement jointly issued by several government agencies. (published 0224 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SINGAPORE'S PEC EXPANDS WORK SCOPE AT EXXONMOBIL PROJECT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 PEC Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Wednesday the value for an existing contract with \f28 \uc2 \f2 ExxonMobil Asia Pacific Pte. Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . has been increased by S$50 million for additional mechanical work at the oil major's facilities on Singapore's Jurong Island. (published 0642 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: TOKYO GAS INTERESTED IN AUSTRALIAN COAL SEAM GAS LNG \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Tokyo Gas Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . is interested in buying liquefied natural gas made from coal seam gas in Australia's Queensland state, a senior company official said Wednesday. (published 0430 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDONESIA GOVT TO SELL UP TO 4M BBL OIL STOCKPILES -OFFICIAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indonesia's government will sell up to 4 million barrels of crude oil from its stockpiles this year, a senior energy official said Wednesday. (published 0312 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: INDONESIA POWER SUPPLY MUST GROW 5,000 MW/YEAR -PLN EXECUTIVE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indonesia's power supply must grow by about 5,000 megawatts a year to support an economic growth rate of 6%, a top executive at the country's state-owned power producer was quoted as saying in an energy ministry statement Wednesday. (published 0503 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SINOPEC\f28 \uc2 \f2  REFINERIES HAVE OPERATED AT LOSS SINCE AUGUST - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China Petroleum & Chemical Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 .'s refineries have been operating at a loss since August because crude oil costs exceed domestic fuel prices, a person familiar with the situation said Wednesday. (published 0248 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =FOCUS: STAKES HIGH FOR WOODSIDE IN PLUTO DRILLING CAMPAIGN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The stakes couldn't be higher for \f28 \uc2 \f2 Woodside Petroleum Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . as it kicks off an expensive campaign to explore for natural gas in Western Australia's offshore Carnarvon basin. (published 0221 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AUSTRALIAN GOVT TO SET UP CENTER FOR RENEWABLE ENERGY - MIN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 An Australian center for renewable energy will be set up to help drive the government's target to source 20% of the nation's power from renewable sources by 2020, Resources & Energy Minister Martin Ferguson said Wednesday. (published 0206 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: NO US-CHINA CLIMATE DEALS DURING OBAMA VISIT-US ENVOY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. Special Envoy for Climate Change Todd Stern said Wednesday he doesn't expect bilateral agreements on global climate issues when U.S. President Barack Obama visits China next month. (published 0335 GMT) [ 28-10-09 0708GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 62550   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020091028e5as000s8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
