\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 1,261 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Oktober 2009\par 08:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: JAPAN RETAIL SALES FALL AS BIG RETAILERS STRUGGLE TO DRAW CUSTOMERS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's overall retail sales declined for the 13th straight month in September with a 1.4% on-year drop, the government said Wednesday, as even super-low-priced own-brand goods struggle to combat low consumer confidence. (published 0413 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: AUSTRALIA 3Q INFLATION ENOUGH TO FUEL RATE HIKE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's consumer price inflation picked up pace in the third quarter, bolstering expectations that the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of Australia\f28 \uc2 \f2  will further raise interest rates at its policy meeting next Tuesday. (published 0408 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par RBA ASST GOV: BANKS ROBUST, WORST NOW WELL OVER FOR ECONOMY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's economy is now well beyond the worst of the global financial crisis and its banking system remains robust and profitable, carrying a minimum of bad loans on its books. (published 0000 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: KOREA CURRENT ACCOUNT SURPLUS DOUBLES IN SEPTEMBER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's current-account surplus more than doubled in September from August, driven by stronger exports and inflows of foreign capital from investors attracted by the country's rapid economic recovery. (published 0340 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE:VIETNAM \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  KEEPING RATE STEADY TILL YEAR-END \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Vietnam's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said Wednesday that it will keep its benchmark rate unchanged for the rest of the year as part of efforts to stabilize the economy, with analysts saying a hike is unlikely until mid-2010. (published 0507 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BANK INDONESIA LIKELY SOLD AROUND $50M BETWEEN IDR9,600 AND IDR9,610 -DEALERS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  likely \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market Wednesday, selling about $50 million in the morning trading session to slow a sharp fall in the rupiah against the U.S. dollar, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dealers said. (published 0414 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE:NOBLE GROUP RAISES US$2.4 BILLION VIA LOAN SYNDICATION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Singapore-listed Noble Group Wednesday said that it has raised US$2.4 billion through loan syndication, making it the largest U.S. dollar syndicated corporate loan in Asia Pacific so far this year. (published 0524 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =DATA SNAP: INDIA SEP INFRASTRUCTURE OUTPUT UP 4.0% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's infrastructure output growth slowed to 4.0% on year in September from 7.8% in August, the government said in a statement Wednesday. (published 0521 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par RBI GOPINATH: COMPULSION TO EXIT EASY POLICY MORE IN INDIA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India may have to exit its easy monetary policy stance before other economies, a deputy governor of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of India\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Wednesday. (published 0455 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par HK GOVERNMENT MAY \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  IN PROPERTY MARKET IF NEEDED - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hong Kong Financial Secretary John Tsang told local property developers Tuesday the government may \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the property market if necessary to protect people's livelihoods and consumers' interests, a person who attended a high-profile meeting between the government and developers said Wednesday. (published 0630 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIAN SKILLED VACANCIES INDEX +1.9% IN OCT VS SEP \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 An index of job vacancies for skilled workers in Australia rose by 1.9% in October from September but still is down 44% from October last year, the Department of Employment and Workplace Relations said Wednesday. (published 0016 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE:NEW ZEALAND OCTOBER BUSINESS CONFIDENCE HOLDING STRONG \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New Zealand's business confidence remained strong in October, according to a survey released Wednesday, reinforcing recent evidence the domestic economy has turned a corner after a protracted recession. (published 0248 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par INDIKA ENERGY SEEKS TO PAY AROUND 9.75% YIELD FOR USD BOND - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indonesia's \f28 \uc2 \f2 PT Indika Energy Tbk\f28 \uc2 \f2 , through its unit Indo Integrated Energy, is looking to pay a yield of around 9.75% for its US$230-million global bond on offer, a person familiar with the deal said Wednesday. (published 0315 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: AGILE PROPERTY TO SELL $400M 7-YEAR USD BOND - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese developer \f28 \uc2 \f2 Agile Property Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . plans to sell US$400 million worth of seven-year U.S. dollar-denominated bonds, a person familiar with the deal said Wednesday. (published 0546 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUCKLAND AIRPORT ANNOUNCES NZ$125 MILLION RETAIL BOND OFFER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Auckland International Airport Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Wednesday it would offer up to NZ$125 million worth of retail bonds. (published 0355 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par MALAYSIA UNVEILS NEW MEASURES FOR AUTO INDUSTRY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Malaysia has announced a raft of measures including lifting a freeze on auto manufacturing licenses and giving new incentives for hybrid electric car making, in bid to make the country an automotive production hub in the region, a government official said Wednesday. (published 0250 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA 1ST-HALF OUTWARD DIRECT INVESTMENT IN AFRICA $875M; UP 78.6% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's outward direct investment in Africa's non-financial sectors rose 78.6% to $875 million in the first half, the highest growth rate for Chinese investment in any geographical region, government data showed. (published 0538 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par THAI \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : COMMERCIAL BANK NPLS 5.7% AT END-SEPTEMBER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Thai commercial banks' gross non-performing loans at the end of September dropped marginally to 5.7% of total loans, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Thailand\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Wednesday. (published 0653 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par INDONESIA MINISTER: AIM TO REDUCE UNEMPLOYMENT BY HALF IN 5 YEARS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indonesia aims to reduce by half its unemployment levels over the next five years through better economic growth, Minister for Manpower and Transmigration Muhaimin Iskandar said. (published 0229 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par DUBAI GOVT USD/AED SUKUK ISSUE OVERSUBSCRIBED - BANKERS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Dubai government's two-part, five-year $2.5 billion bond has been oversubscribed, bankers familiar with the deal told Zawya Dow Jones Wednesday. (published 0637 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par      ======== DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======== \par  \par  \par =WORLD \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 :EURO HITS 1-WK LOW VS YEN ON RENEWED RISK AVERSION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The euro fell to a one-week low against the yen in Asia on Wednesday as weak regional share prices prompted investors to decrease their holdings of the risk-sensitive unit. (published 0534 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  OPTIONS: EURO/YEN OPTIONS UP; FURTHER RISE EXPECTED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Euro/yen \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  options rose in Asia Wednesday as the underlying rate declined, prodding investors into buying protection against further falls in the euro. (published 0255 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =CHARTING ASIA: DOLLAR MAY RISE TO CHF1.0355, CHF1.0452 N/T \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The U.S. dollar fell sharply against other major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Wednesday immediately after some stronger-than-expected Australian inflation data, but it soon bounced back, exposing the strong underlying demand for the greenback. Against the Swiss franc in particular, technical charts are flagging further gains for the dollar to CHF1.0355, and possibly CHF1.0452, in the near term. (published 0229 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =PREVIEW: KOREA TRADE SURPLUS LIKELY $2 BILLION IN OCTOBER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's trade surplus likely shrank in October from a month earlier as exports were relatively sluggish due to fewer working days in the month, while imports rose following gains in global oil and raw-material prices, economists said. (published 0659 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =PREVIEW: KOREA INDUSTRIAL OUTPUT LIKELY UP 6.8% IN SEPTEMBER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's industrial output probably rose at its fastest pace in more than a year in September due to increased demand ahead of Chusok holidays, with carmakers and chip makers likely to have led the way, economists said. (published 0241 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =MONEY TALKS: YIELD WON'T BE A MAJOR FRIEND FOR THE US DOLLAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The U.S. dollar is coming up for air. But probably not for long. The hardcore selling of the greenback in recent weeks has tapered off, with the euro in particular giving back a little ground and higher risk \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  like the Australian dollar looking a bit toppish. But don't presume this will be a major respite. (published 0003 GMT) [ 28-10-09 0700GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020091028e5as000qk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
