\par\par \b \uc2 Dow Jones Asia-Pacific Top Stories Sked For October 22\b0\par\par\uc2 2,124 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Oktober 2009\par 09:08\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Following are the top Asia-Pacific stories featured on Dow Jones Newswires as of 0700 GMT. Not all stories appear on all wires. Please direct any questions or comments to asianewseds@dowjones.com.\par \par \uc2 MACRO/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /FIXED INCOME:\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par =2ND UPDATE: CHINA DATA RAISE LIKELIHOOD OF POLICY TWEAKS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The continued pickup in China's economic growth in the third quarter raises the likelihood that Beijing will begin to tweak its stimulus policies next year, as it turns its attention toward the risks of excess capacity and inflation. (published 0435 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN REFORM MINISTER SENGOKU: FISCAL 2009 TAX REVENUE COULD BE SHARPLY BELOW Y40T \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese administrative reform minister Yoshito Sengoku said Thursday that the government's tax revenue could fall well below Y40 trillion in the current fiscal year ending March, adding to worries that Tokyo may end up selling a record Y50 trillion or more of new debt in the year. (published 0230 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: JAPAN TRADE SURPLUS HIGHEST IN 18 MONTHS, BUT GROWTH LIKELY TO SLOW \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's merchandise trade surplus expanded to its largest level in 18 months in September, with the decline in exports slowing as overseas markets picked up somewhat, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said Thursday. (published 0252 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AUSTRALIA TSY SECY: ECONOMY SHOWING ENCOURAGING SIGNS OF RECOVERY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's Treasury Secretary Ken Henry said Thursday that the domestic economy is showing "encouraging signs" of recovery. (published 0351 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AUSTRALIA TRADE MIN: AUSTRALIAN DOLLAR RISE COMMODITY-DRIVEN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A strengthening Australian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is being driven by rising commodity prices, Trade Minister Simon Crean said Thursday. (published 0138 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: AUSTRALIAN BANK WATCHDOG NOT YET SCALING BACK SCRUTINY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Banking regulator the Australian Prudential Regulation Authority said Thursday it isn't yet ready to scale back the level of regulatory scrutiny that was stepped up as the global financial crisis unfolded. (published 0640 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: VIETNAM \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : NOT DEVALUING DONG -REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Vietnam isn't devaluing the dong but flexibly adjusting its dollar exchange rate after the local unit rose to record this week, threatening to hurt growth at a time when exports and remittances have slumped. (published 0429 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: BANK OF KOREA TO STOP BUYING BANK DEBENTURES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Korea said Thursday it will end a one-year program to buy bank debentures and other special-purpose bonds introduced last November to help supply liquidity into the financial system. (published 0337 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par S KOREA:NOT MULLING MEASURES ON FOREIGN BANKS' \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  LIQUIDITY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The South Korean government isn't considering imposing any new measures on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  liquidity of foreign banks operating in the country, an official from the Ministry of Strategy and Finance said Thursday, refuting recent media reports. (published 0309 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN FSA TO EXTEND SMALLER FIRMS NEW CREDIT LINE UP TO 3 YEARS-NIKKEI \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's Financial Services Agency said it will establish a fund to provide fresh lines of credit to cash-strapped small and midsize companies, whose debts are not covered by public loans and credit facilities, the Nikkei reported Thursday. (published 0327 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AUSTRALIA'S APRA: NOT READY TO SCALE BACK REGULATORY SCRUTINY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Banking regulator the Australian Prudential Regulation Authority said Thursday it isn't yet ready to scale back the level of regulatory scrutiny that was stepped up as the global financial crisis unfolded. (published 0622 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par HKMA SELLS HK$5.04 BLN TO DEFEND US DLR PEG THURSDAY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Hong Kong \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said Thursday it sold HK$5.04 billion in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market to defend the Hong Kong dollar's peg to the U.S. dollar. (published 0313 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BANK INDONESIA SUSPECTED SOLD $50M TO SUPPORT RUPIAH -DEALERS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was suspected to have \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to arrest a slide in the rupiah Thursday, selling at least $50 million to prevent the dollar from breaking a key resistance of IDR9,500, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dealers said. (published 0544 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =DATA SNAP: INDIA WPI UP 1.21% ON YEAR IN WEEK ENDED OCT 10 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's inflation rate rose to 1.21% in the week ended Oct. 10 from 0.92% in the previous week, the Ministry of Commerce and Industry said Thursday. (published 0649 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: INDIA TO CHECK CO2 EMISSIONS; SEEKS TECH HELP, FUNDS -PM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India will aim to keep its per-capita carbon emissions below the level of developed nations, Prime Minister Manmohan Singh said Thursday, but he stressed that richer countries should be offering the funds and technology needed to fight climate change. (published 0646 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 DOWNER EDI\f28 \uc2 \f2  RAISES A$150M FROM MEDIUM TERM NOTE ISSUE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australian engineering firm \f28 \uc2 \f2 Downer EDI Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Thursday it raised A$150 million from the issue of medium-term notes priced at 375 basis points over swap after the offer closed oversubscribed. (published 0059 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: AUSTRALIA FUTURE FUND: GLOBAL BANK SECTOR STILL FACES RISKS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's Future Fund Chairman David Murray said Thursday the financial system has reached a point of "reasonable" stability but that the global banking sector still faces risks. (published 0436 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AUSTRALIA WANTS TO BOOST TRADE IN SERVICES WITH JAPAN - MINISTER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia wants to use negotiations over a free trade agreement with Japan to boost trade in services, Trade Minister Simon Crean said Thursday ahead of a visit to Japan on Sunday through Tuesday. (published 0422 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDONESIA BEHIND SCHEDULE ON INFRASTRUCTURE STIMULUS - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indonesia's government has spent only about a quarter of the fiscal stimulus allocated for infrastructure development this year, the Jakarta Globe reported Thursday, citing official data. (published 0404 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDONESIA PLN HIRES BARCLAYS, \f28 \uc2 \f2 UBS\f28 \uc2 \f2  TO MANAGE DOLLAR BOND SALE-SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indonesian state-owned utility \f28 \uc2 \f2 PT Perusahaan Listrik Negara\f28 \uc2 \f2  has hired \f28 \uc2 \f2 Barclays Capital\f28 \uc2 \f2  and UBS AG to manage its planned fixed-rate U.S. dollar-denominated global bond sale, a person familiar with the deal said Thursday. (published 0229 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AXIS BANK TO MEET INVESTORS, MAY SELL DOLLAR BOND - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Axis Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  plans to sell a benchmark-sized dollar-denominated bond offshore after meeting investors in a road show scheduled for next week, a person familiar with the Indian bank's plans said Thursday. (published 0619 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par THAICOM SETS COUPON ON 3-YEAR BONDS AT 5.25%, 5-YEAR BONDS AT 6.15% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Thaicom PCL\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Thursday it would pay a coupon of 5.25% on the three-year bonds it plans to issue and 6.15% on a five-year tranche. (published 0340 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 4Q HIRING EXPECTATIONS RISE IN CHINA, HK, SINGAPORE - SURVEY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 More employers in China, Hong Kong and Singapore plan to increase hiring in the fourth quarter, in line with growing optimism about economic recovery, a quarterly survey by recruitment agency \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hudson Highland Group Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . showed Thursday. (published 0630 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  OPTIONS: YEN OPTIONS DOWN; COULD RISE ANYTIME IF DOLLAR SURGES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Dollar/yen \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  options fell in Asia Thursday as demand for hedges decreased due to narrowly-traded spot rates, and dealers said the volatilities will keep declining, though the chance of a sudden surge remains. (published 0358 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =INTERVIEW:ASIA CORPORATE LOANS MAY TAKE 2 YRS TO RECOVER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 As the region continues to recover from the financial crisis, bank lending to Asian companies, other than those in China and Japan, won't grow at "meaningful" levels for around two years, although local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 -loan markets have been developing as a source of funding, said \f28 \uc2 \f2 Citigroup Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 .'s most senior investment banker in Asia. (published 0324 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =PREVIEW: SINGAPORE SEPTEMBER CPI LIKELY DOWN 0.1% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Singapore's consumer prices likely fell for a sixth consecutive month in September mainly due to the high base of a year earlier. (published 0501 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 EQUITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par =2ND UPDATE: KNOC BOOSTS RESERVES WITH HARVEST ENERGY DEAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 State-run Korea National Oil Corp., or KNOC, is to buy Canada's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Harvest Energy Trust\f28 \uc2 \f2  for C$4.1 billion in the latest in a string of acquisitions by resource-poor Asian countries trying to bolster their energy security. (published 0501 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AU OPTRONICS 3RD-QUARTER NET PROFIT SOARS TO NT$7.42 BLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 AU Optronics Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . reported Thursday a net profit for the three months ended Sept. 30 of NT$7.42 billion, more than eight times its net profit in the same period last year of NT$860 million, boosted by record shipments of large-sized panels. (published 0559 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par HYUNDAI 3Q NET SOARS ON NEW CARS, STRONG OVERSEAS SALES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hyundai Motor Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Thursday its net profit more than tripled in the third quarter on robust demand for new models and strong overseas sales. (published 0459 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TOKYO ELECTRON SEES SMALLER 1H GROUP NET LOSS Y16.10B \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Tokyo Electron Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Thursday it now estimates a smaller-than-expected net loss for the half ended Sept. 30, due to a pickup in sales of chip-making equipment and cost reductions. (published 0651 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: AMCOR EXPECTS ALCAN PACKAGING DEAL TO CLOSE BY JANUARY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Amcor Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . \f28 \uc2 \f2 Chief Executive Ken MacKenzie\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Thursday he expects U.S. and European regulators to approve its A$2.44 billion acquisition of parts of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Rio Tinto Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 .'s Alcan packaging business by January. (published 0522 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: AUSTAR 3Q EARNINGS RISE AS SALES, MARGINS IMPROVE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Regional pay television group \f28 \uc2 \f2 Austar United Communications Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Thursday that its third quarter earnings rose 12% from a year earlier on the back of a 6% increase in revenue and improved margins. (published 0103 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: TEN TIPS IMPROVING AD MARKET; REPORTS FY LOSS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 22-10-09 0708GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australian television and media group \f28 \uc2 \f2 Ten Network Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Thursday that there are "clear signs" of an improvement in the advertising market in another signal that the Australian market may have bottomed. (published 0522 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =2NDUPDATE:HERO HONDA:CHALLENGE TO KEEP FIRST HALF EBITDA MARGIN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hero Honda Motors Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Thursday said it may find it difficult to sustain its current profit margin in the second half of the financial year through March due to rising raw material prices. (published 0657 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE:BIOCON SECOND QUARTER NET PROFIT ALMOST TRIPLES TO INR741.9M \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Biocon Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Thursday said its second quarter net profit almost tripled from a year earlier, helped by higher revenue at both its biopharmaceuticals and contract research businesses and a lower base last year when it had \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  losses. (published 0609 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 LARSEN & TOUBRO\f28 \uc2 \f2  2Q NET PROFIT INR5.80B VS INR4.60B \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Larsen & Toubro Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Thursday said second quarter net profit rose 26%, helped by exceptional gains during the quarter. (published 0639 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: EVERONN EXPECTS REVENUE TO DOUBLE IN FISCAL 2010 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Everonn Education Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . expects revenue to double in the current fiscal year as it expands \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and because of higher government spending on education, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Managing Director P. Kishore\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Thursday. (published 0644 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ENERGY/COMMODITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par =UPDATE: OIL DATA: CHINA 4TH-QUARTER CRUDE RUNS MAY STAY HIGH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's crude runs will likely remain at high levels in the fourth quarter amid expectations domestic demand for oil products will strengthen tracking faster economic growth, analysts said Thursday. (published 0317 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: COAL DATA: CHINA SEP COAL,POWER OUTPUT UP; HIGH DEMAND \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's September coal output rose marginally versus August, while power output grew at a record 9.5% from a year ago, according to data from the National Bureau of Statistics Thursday. (published 0633 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: OIL DATA: JAPAN CRUDE OIL DEMAND LIKELY TO REMAIN WEAK \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's imports of crude oil and condensate in September fell 2.9% from a year earlier, moderating from consecutive double-digit declines in February-August, data from the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  showed Thursday. (published 0235 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: INDIA TO CHECK CO2 EMISSIONS; SEEKS TECH HELP, FUNDS -PM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India will aim to keep its per-capita carbon emissions below the level of developed nations, Prime Minister Manmohan Singh said Thursday, but he stressed that richer countries should be offering the funds and technology needed to fight climate change. (published 0646 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =CHINA SEPTEMBER CRUDE STEEL OUTPUT SECOND HIGHEST MONTHLY IN 2009 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's crude steel production in September was this year's second-highest volume, underscoring the formidable odds stacked against the government's campaign to slim down the industry for the country's long-term economic health. (published 0259 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TOCOM RSS3 RUBBER FUTURES RISE ABOVE Y230/KG; ONE-YEAR HIGH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Natural rubber futures on the Tokyo Commodity Exchange breached key resistance of Y230 per kilogram to reach a new one-year high Thursday on strong buying and spillover support from higher crude oil, trade participants said. (published 0416 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDIA MAY ALLOW 10,000 TONS OF EDIBLE OIL EXPORTS IN 2009-10 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India is planning to allow the export of 10,000 metric tons of edible oil in the marketing year starting November, a government official said Thursday. (published 0554 GMT) [ 22-10-09 0708GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 62550   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020091022e5am000oe\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
