\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE: Bank Indonesia: IDR Gains In Line With Regional Peers\b0\par\par\uc2 418 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Oktober 2009\par 10:01\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 (Adds central banker's comments on inflation, loan growth; updates rupiah level; background.)\par \par \uc2 By Farida Husna and Reuben Carder\par \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES\par \par \uc2 JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--The rupiah's recent strong gains against the dollar are in line with the strength of regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and with domestic economic fundamentals, Bank Indonesia Acting Governor Darmin Nasution said Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 "The rupiah isn't alone. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of other countries around us are also strengthening," Nasution said, adding that Bank Indonesia will work to curb excessive volatility in the exchange rate.\par \par \uc2 Nasution's remarks came after Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  was suspected to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  quite heavily to support the dollar last week.\par \par \uc2 Analysts expect Bank Indonesia to tolerate gains in the rupiah but predict it will step in from time to time to buy the U.S. dollar, to curb intraday falls in the greenback that it deems too sharp. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  generally favours a stronger rupiah to help fight inflation, and this concern outweighs that of export competitiveness, analysts say.\par \par \uc2 Nasution said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  aims to prevent local businesses from being adversely affected by sharp \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements. However, he said Bank Indonesia doesn't consider any particular level for the rupiah against the dollar as "comfortable." Bank Indonesia does consider the impact of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements on importers, exporters and the government, he said, without elaborating.\par \par \uc2 The government uses a forecast average exchange rate to calculate \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  related costs in the state budget each year. He said the dollar will likely average IDR10,000 or higher against the rupiah this year, despite a significant fall below that level in the second half of the year.\par \par \uc2 The dollar Wednesday fetched around IDR9,365, lower than IDR9,445 at Tuesday's close. The rupiah has gained more than 17% against the greenback since January.\par \par \uc2 Nasution also said that inflation is likely to return to the "normal range" of around 4% to 6% next year, and reiterated Bank Indonesia's forecast for inflation this year to be 4% or lower. Consumer prices rose 11.1% in 2008.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, loan growth this year will likely be around 11%, below a 15% level that Bank Indonesia considers as the minimum level to support economic growth, Nasution said. As for next year, loans are expected to rise at a faster pace, he added.\par \par \uc2 -By Farida Husna and Reuben Carder, Dow Jones Newswires; 62 21 3983 1277; Reuben.Carder@dowjones.com [ 14-10-09 0801GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020091014e5ae000p1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
