\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: USD/IDR Ends Lower; 9,350-9,450 Tipped Thursday\b0\par\par\uc2 1,191 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Oktober 2009\par 11:07\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; \par MarketTalk@dowjones.com \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0907 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/IDR ends lower at 9,375 vs 9,445 last close on USD's general weakness, dealers say. "There was no sign of Bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  today, but it may buy the dollar tomorrow if the greenback falls to IDR9,350," a dealer says; the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's acting governor Darmin Nasution says IDR's recent strong gains vs USD in line with strength of regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and with domestic economic fundamentals; adds will work to curb excessive volatility in the exchange rate; 9,350-9,450 tipped tomorrow. (IMS)\f28 \par \par \uc2 0905 GMT [Dow Jones] Five-year senior CDS spreads written on financials Credit Agricole (ACA.FR) and RBS (RBS) fail to move sharply Wednesday, quoted slightly tighter at 84bps versus 86bps Tuesday, and 107bps versus 110bps, according to CMA DataVision. Credit Agricole says it will use funds from recent bond issues to help it reimburse EUR3 billion worth of state aid issued at the height of the financial crisis in December 2008. While RBS says it may give up 312 branches. (SYC)\par \par \uc2 0852 GMT [Dow Jones] HKD IRS down 1-4 bps across sectors, curve flattens, mirroring U.S. counterpart, says \uc2 HSBC\uc2 . "The sensitivity to U.S. Treasurys reflects the open nature of Asia's capital markets...(and) the importance of the U.S. dollar in trade, bank balance sheets and \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves." Flush liquidity also keeps short-ends low, HKD 1-year IRS down 2 bps at 0.51%, 2-year down 1 bp at 1.17%; 5-year down 3 bps at 2.47%, 10-year down 4 bps at 3.08%. (ARP)\par \par \uc2 0851 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/MYR at fresh 2009 low late of 3.3700 vs yesterday's close at 3.3890; dealer with local brokerage says pair down on dollar weakness, improving risk appetite, moves in line with USD/Asians. "Selling pressure on the U.S. dollar remained strong throughout the day, but we are seeing a little support at the 3.3700 level," says dealer, adds likely improved corporate results from U.S. in coming days may keep dollar under pressure. Tips next major support at 3.3500, if 3.3700 breached. (KPL)\par \par \uc2 0845 GMT [Dow Jones] China onshore IRS consolidate after recent sharp gains. 1-year down 1 bp at 2.02%-2.07%, 5-year +1 bp at 3.44%-3.49%, 1-to-5-year spread 2 bps wider at 142 bps. But Shanghai-based foreign bank expects swaps to rise more in near future on strong stocks (Shanghai Composite Index ends +1.2% at 2970.53), higher-than-expected credit data. China's September new yuan loans total CNY516.7 billion, vs August's CNY410.4 billion, CNY450 billion expected. (WYL)\par \par \uc2 0840 GMT [Dow Jones] Gilts remain firmly entrenched in negative territory Wednesday, marking fresh intraday lows after the latest UK labor market data. The jobless claimant count rises by 20,800 in September, versus forecast +25,000, while the ILO unemployment rate remains at 7.9% in the three months to August, versus forecast 8.0%. The December gilt futures contract is currently down 0.53 on the day at 119.87, from around 119.94 prior to the numbers and versus a session low of 119.86. The 10-year benchmark gilt is down 0.45 at 108.355, yielding 3.45%, from around 3.445% prior to the data. (KJE)\par \par \uc2 0839 GMT [Dow Jones] Next key level for USD/INR (after break of 46.80) is 45.79, which is 61.8% Fibonacci retracement of up-move from 41.83 to 52.19, says Standard Chartered Bank; notes, pace of recent moves has increased risk of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but still thinks "such concerns are overdone." Says, "The RBI has never really indicated that it prefers an undervalued \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and as such, we do not believe that it will prevent INR appreciation if the USD collapses against key trading-partner \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." USD/INR last 46.1500. (SDS)\par \par \uc2 0836 GMT [Dow Jones] \uc2 Citigroup\uc2  says the zloty is on track to climb over the medium term, with privatization plans, widening rate differentials, economic recovery and moderate PLN undervaluation all pointing to a climb. But "there is no obvious reason for near-term outperformance," the bank says. Investors are already quite heavily exposed to PLN through government bond holdings, bank notes. EUR/PLN trades at 4.2078. (KJM)\par \par \uc2 0834 GMT [Dow Jones] Sterling gains after August jobs data came in better than expected. The claimant count was +20.8K against expectations of a 25k rise and the unemployment rate stayed at 7.9% instead of the expected rise to 8%. GBP/USD trades up some 40 ticks to 1.5980 and EUR/GBP drops to the day's low of 0.9309. (GST)\par \par \uc2 0833 GMT [Dow Jones] PREVIEW: India WPI likely to rise 1.46% on year in week to October 3 vs 0.70% increase previous week, indicates Dow Jones poll of 5 economists. "A combination of strong festive season demand and a weakening base effect should push the inflation rate higher," says economist at state-run bank; RBI Governor Subbarao recently said RBI may have to reverse its easy monetary stance earlier than most other countries as inflationary pressures mounting quickly. Data due 0630 GMT Thursday. (NEC)\par \par \uc2 0831 GMT [Dow Jones] US Treasurys edge broadly lower in London Wednesday as European equity markets advance following Intel's better-than-expected 3Q earnings report. On the data front, September retail sales, forecast -2.1%, ex-autos seen +0.3%, and September import prices, forecast +0.3%, are due at 1230 GMT. August business inventories, expected -1.2%, are due at 1400 GMT, ahead of the release of the September FOMC meeting minutes at 1800 GMT. The Treasury yield curve moves marginally flatter, with the 2-year/10-year benchmark spread narrowing to +243.0bp from Tuesday's +243.5bp. The 2-year note is down 1/32 at 100 5/32, yielding 0.92%, the 10-year down 3+/32 at 102 8+/32, yielding 3.35%, with the 30-year bond unchanged at 105 8/32, yielding 4.19%. Bunds and gilts move lower ahead of supply. December bunds are down 0.35 at 122.20, with December gilts down 0.45 at 119.95. (KJE)\par \par \uc2 0829 GMT [Dow Jones] China's September new yuan loans total CNY516.7 billion, vs August's CNY410.4 billion, CNY450 billion expected, with data likely to assuage worries Beijing is reining in credit too quickly; if anything, suggests \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is still supporting economic growth, despite recent talk by PBOC Vice Gov. Yi Gang that it'll guard against hidden risks like inflation. Meanwhile \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, world's largest, continued to rise in July-September (up average $47 billion for each month in 3Q, vs $59 billion average in 2Q), hitting $2.273 trillion at end- September.(TPX) [ 10-14-09 0507ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020091014e5ae0006r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
