\par\par \b \uc2 IMF Indonesia rep says strong rupiah can help contain inflation\b0\par\par\uc2 207 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Oktober 2009\par 08:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 JAKARTA, Oct 14 (Reuters) - The appreciation of Indonesia's rupiah <IDR=> could help contain price pressure in Southeast Asia's biggest economy, the International Monetary Fund's senior resident representative in Indonesia said on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Milan Zavadjil, the IMF's representative, also told Reuters in an email that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BI), was right to direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to trying to reduce volatility in the rupiah, which is Asia's best-performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  so far this year.\par \par \uc2 "In the current situation of strong capital inflows, the appreciation of the rupiah can help contain domestic price rises. BI is right to direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  largely at reducing volatility," he said.\par \par \uc2 Zavadjil noted that the country's exchange rate flexibility has helped it in the past to deal with large capital flows.\par \par \uc2 "Exchange rate flexibility has served as an important shock absorber for Indonesia," he said.\par \par \uc2 "During the worse of the global financial crisis, the flexibility of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  helped absorb large capital outflows, thus avoiding a large loss in reserves and a loss in confidence." (Reporting by Gde Anugrah Arka, Editing by Sara Webb)\par \par \uc2 INDONESIA-ECONOMY/IMF (URGENT)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|IF|M|D   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020091014e5ae000ec\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
