\par\par \b \uc2 =DJ  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  ASIA:Bank Indonesia Will Let Rupiah Rise At Measured Pace\b0\par\par\uc2 By Reuben Carder  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 557 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 September 2009\par 07:43\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2009, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--The rupiah's rally is good for Indonesia's economy and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  knows it. That's why it will let the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rise further - at a measured pace.\par \par \uc2 The rupiah has climbed nearly 4% against the dollar this month and almost 15% since January as investors have piled into Southeast Asia's largest economy on hopes that an improved political and security environment and the country's new, investor-friendly government will lead to large returns on Indonesian stocks and other investments.\par \par \uc2 The dollar's broad decline has added to rupiah bullishness.\par \par \uc2 With its large domestic market, Indonesia relies much less on exports to drive economic growth than many of its Asian peers, so there's not much pressure to drive the rupiah down to get an edge on Malaysia, the Philippines and Thailand, its rivals in palm oil, natural rubber, timber, metals and other exports.\par \par \uc2 Indonesia's exports amount to about one third of gross domestic product and net exports less than 2%. In Thailand, exports make up around two thirds of GDP.\par \par \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to slow the rupiah's rise, but the dollar-buying clearly isn't aimed at trying to change the market's direction. Acting Gov. Darmin Nasution said earlier this month merely that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't want the rupiah to strengthen "too fast."\par \par \uc2 Analysts say Bank Indonesia would allow the dollar to fall to IDR9,200-IDR9,300 - the top of a range of IDR8,700-IDR9,300 that prevailed for nearly three years before the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  spiked last year when the global financial crisis deepened.\par \par \uc2 The dollar was at IDR9,730 Monday at 0520 GMT.\par \par \uc2 "The rupiah will be among the top performers in the region - the only limiting factor is the fact that it has strengthened so much this year," said Gundy Cahyadi, an economist at IdeaGlobal in Singapore. Indonesia is "not as dependent on exports as Thailand or Malaysia - that's the advantage."\par \par \uc2 Cahyadi forecast the dollar will fall below IDR9,500 and could test IDR9,400 by the end of the year.\par \par \uc2 Fauzi Ichsan, an economist at Standard Chartered in Jakarta, said Bank Indonesia might start buying dollars under IDR9,500 but that it will only look to slow the rupiah's rise, not stop it.\par \par \uc2 A strong rupiah would keep imported inflation in check, which could be key to curbing price pressures in a world of rising commodity and energy prices.\par \par \uc2 What's more, Indonesia's newly reelected president, Susilo Bambang Yudhoyono, plans to build up the country's infrastructure to lay a firmer foundation for lasting economic growth. A strong rupiah makes imported capital goods cheaper.\par \par \uc2 Jakarta has pledged to spend more on infrastructure as it aims to bring economic growth up to about 5% in 2010 from an estimated 4.3% this year.\par \par \uc2 Not all analysts think the rupiah's strength will last. ING forecasts the dollar will rise to IDR10,500 by the end of the year as inflationary expectations turn investors away from local assets.\par \par \uc2 -By Reuben Carder, Dow Jones Newswires; 62 21 3983 1277; Reuben.Carder@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 September 28, 2009 01:43 ET (05:43 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020090928e59s000j6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
