\par\par \b \uc2 *DJ Bk Indonesia Official: Remain Consistent On Monetary Policy\b0\par\par\uc2 332 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Juni 2009\par 15:27\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2009, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 24 Jun 2009 09:29 EDT *DJ  Bank Indonesia: To Enhance Effectiveness Of Fiscal Stimulus\par \par \uc2 24 Jun 2009 09:31 EDT *DJ  Bank Indonesia: Domestic Banks' Credit May Grow 15% This Yr\par \par \uc2 24 Jun 2009 09:34 EDT *DJ  Bank Indonesia: Urge Domestic Banks To Lower Lending Rates\par \par \uc2 24 Jun 2009 09:35 EDT *DJ  Bank Indonesia: To Combat Volatility In Exchange Rate\par \par \uc2 24 Jun 2009 09:37 EDT *DJ  Bank Indonesia: Local Banks' Credit Began Rebounding In Apr\par \par \uc2 24 Jun 2009 09:54 EDT DJ  Bk Indonesia Official: Remain Consistent On Monetary Policy\par \par \uc2 JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--Bank Indonesia will remain consistent on monetary policy and will work to support the domestic economy, a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official said late Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will support the local economy by "accelerating the absorption of the government's fiscal stimulus package," Wimboh Santoso, Bank Indonesia head of bureau for financial stability, told an awards ceremony.\par \par \uc2 He said Bank Indonesia's 2.5-percentage-point cut to its policy rate since December should encourage local banks to give more loans, and at lower rates.\par \par \uc2 Santoso said that, despite an ongoing freeze in the domestic credit market since late last year, banks' credit has shown signs of growth since April. Local banks' credit growth may reach 15% this year, only slightly lower than around 17% in 2008, Santoso said.\par \par \uc2 He added that "Bank Indonesia will also work to minimize exchange rate volatility," indicating the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will continue its recent policy of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent weeks has resumed meaningful \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, selling around $100 million or more on at least one day, after mostly avoiding large \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since late last year, according to \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers.\par \par \uc2 -By Linda Silaen and Reuben Carder, Dow Jones Newswires; 62 21 3983 1277; Reuben.Carder@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 June 24, 2009 09:54 ET (13:54 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020090624e56o0038p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
