\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Indonesia c.bank says to use "ammunition" on rupiah\b0\par\par\uc2 265 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Februar 2009\par 04:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  (Adds details)\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, Feb 18 (Reuters) - Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor said on Wednesday that Bank Indonesia was prepared to use its ammunition to support the rupiah <IDR=>, after further weakness in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2  The rupiah dropped as low as 12,000 per dollar on Wednesday morning, down nearly 1 percent from Tuesday's close.\par \par \uc2  "The dollar is strengthening against other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . We will guard so that we will not have too much volatility, but we are following global movements," said Boediono, who uses only one name like many Indonesians.\par \par \uc2  "We are always in the market, we will use the ammunition that we have and we will add to our ammunition" to support the rupiah, he said without elaborating.\par \par \uc2  The Indonesian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has lost around 8 percent versus the dollar so far this year, the second worst performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Asia after the South Korean won, which has fallen 13 percent.\par \par \uc2  Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been weakening as deepening worries about a global recession has prompted investors to shed riskier assets, with the won and the rupiah bearing the brunt of the selling.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent months to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , or at least limit the fall in the rupiah.\par \par \uc2  The country's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves hade fallen to $50.87 billion by the end of January, down from around $57 billion in September.  (Writing by Tyagita Silka; Editing by Ed Davies)  \par \par \uc2 INDONESIA-ECONOMY/RUPIAH (UPDATE)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|IF|ABX|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020090218e52i0005q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
