\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE: Bank Indonesia Surprises With 25 BPs Policy Rate Cut\b0\par\par\uc2 620 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Dezember 2008\par 09:09\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 (Adds details, background, and economists' comments)\par \par \uc2 JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--The Indonesian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Thursday surprised the market by cutting its benchmark rate by 25 basis points, a move that analysts say highlights its proactive stance in mitigating the impact of the global slowdown on the domestic economy.\par \par \uc2 "The rate cut to 9.25% is expected to stimulate business activities amid the global economic slowdown," Bank Indonesia said in a press release after a monthly rate-setting meeting.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  added that it expects inflationary pressures to continue easing in the coming months, paving the way for further cuts.\par \par \uc2 Consumer-price inflation eased to 0.12% on month in November from 0.45% in October, and to 11.68% on year from 11.77%.\par \par \uc2 Bank Indonesia said that it expects annual inflation to continue sliding to around 6.5% next year thanks to falling commodity and energy prices in the international markets.\par \par \uc2 Nine out of 12 economists polled by Dow Jones Newswires had expected Bank Indonesia to hold the rate steady, citing concerns about the rupiah, which has lost 24% of its value against the dollar so far this year.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also cut the overnight repurchase rate it offers to commercial banks to 9.75% from 10.50%, and increased its overnight deposit rate to 8.75% from 8.50% in an effort to "resolve the segmentations in the interbank money market."\par \par \uc2 Shifting Focus\par \par \uc2 Analysts said that the cut in the policy rate, the first since December 2007, indicates the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's focus is shifting toward spurring growth and away from controlling inflation.\par \par \uc2 "Not surprisingly, this...decision was justified on the basis of more gloomy domestic and international growth prospects as well as greater confidence that inflation will fall within (if not below) the 6.5%-7.5% target range of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Robert Prior-Wandesforde, a Singapore-based economist with \uc2 HSBC\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Growth in Southeast Asia's largest economy slowed slightly to 6.11% on year in the third quarter of the year from 6.39% during the April-June quarter.\par \par \uc2 Finance Minister Sri Mulyani Indrawati said last month that growth would likely continue sliding, to between 4.5% and 5% in 2009 as demand for Indonesia's exports would be hurt by recession in major economies.\par \par \uc2 Analysts said that the rate decision could also signal that Bank Indonesia is of the view that interest rates are no longer effective in defending the rupiah.\par \par \uc2 The rupiah was trading at IDR12,050 to the dollar at 0725 GMT, slightly higher than its Wednesday close of IDR12,250 as year-end demand for dollars from local companies eased, dealers say.\par \par \uc2 "There was no knee-jerk reaction against the rate cut as it is minor compared with the cuts done by other central banks," a dealer with a foreign bank in Jakarta said.\par \par \uc2 In a sign that it acknowledges the rate cut could make the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  less attractive, Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  said that it will continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to reduce the volatility in the rupiah.\par \par \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been actively \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market since October as the rupiah fell to its lowest level in a decade.\par \par \uc2 Analysts said that Indonesia needs to secure loan commitments from multilateral and bilateral lenders in order to improve confidence in the local unit.\par \par \uc2 The government has approached the World Bank, Asian Development Bank, Islamic Development Bank, Japan, France and Australia recently, but so far there has been no commitment from those potentials lenders.\par \par \uc2 -By Farida Husna and I Made Sentana, Dow Jones Newswires; 62 21 39831277; I-Made.Sentana@dowjones.com [ 04-12-08 0809GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020081204e4c4000ae\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or operation*) and (indonesia near10 interven*) and (rst=trtw or rst=tprw or rst=tdjw) and (central bank or ministry of finance or treasury ministry or monetary authority)\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Datum\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 01/01/1995 bis 21/08/2023\cell \pard \ql \li0\r